ing relationship or classification. Evidence to use: surveys sent through digital means to respondents; respondents also reply to the survey digitally", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_ELECTRONIC_SURVEYS_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_315_03576C"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_A1262E4C", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"If you applied this claim about electronic surveys to a different product, customer group, or organization, what evidence would you check before accepting it, and what result would make you reject it?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:38.912Z'), rung:2, rationale:"Transfers the identified reasoning error to a new marketing decision while requiring a falsifiable check rather than copying the claim: Online distribution removes all coverage and nonresponse biases.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_ELECTRONIC_SURVEYS_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_315_03576C"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_A987E134", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"The source evidence is: method of collecting data that is conducted by observing people’s natural behavior Which concrete detail contradicts this claim about ethnographic research: A brief laboratory questionnaire is equivalent to observing behavior in its natural setting.", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:38.912Z'), rung:0, rationale:"Requires a concrete source detail that falsifies the stated assumption about ethnographic research.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_ETHNOGRAPHIC_RESEARCH_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_3_F047F6"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_24D6C7E4", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"Using the framework of steps in a successful marketing research plan, how would you explain ethnographic research correctly, and which distinction does the flawed claim erase?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:38.912Z'), rung:1, rationale:"Re-establishes the relevant marketing relationship or classification. E