 appearance while ignoring product and service needs.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_ADAPTATION_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_400_01969B"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_3CBB6067", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"The source evidence is: third largest multicultural group in the United States; made up of 22 different subethnicities from the Asian continent, Hawaii, and islands of the Pacific; can belong to a single race or mixed races Which concrete detail contradicts this claim about asian population: Asian consumers form one culturally homogeneous market with identical languages and preferences.", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:38.912Z'), rung:0, rationale:"Requires a concrete source detail that falsifies the stated assumption about asian population.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_ASIAN_POPULATION_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_401_332CEA"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_9E847DA3", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"Using the framework of marketing to hispanic, black, and asian consumers, how would you explain asian population correctly, and which distinction does the flawed claim erase?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:38.912Z'), rung:1, rationale:"Re-establishes the relevant marketing relationship or classification. Evidence to use: third largest multicultural group in the United States; made up of 22 different subethnicities from the Asian continent, Hawaii, and islands of the Pacific; can belong to a single race or mixed races", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_ASIAN_POPULATION_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_401_332CEA"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_4AEFDC67", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"If you applied this claim about asian population to a different product, customer group, or organization, what evidence would you check before accepting it, and what result would make you reject it?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:38.912Z'), rung:2, rationale:"Transfers the identified reasoning error to a new marketing decision while requiring a falsifiable check rather than copying the claim: Asian consumers form one culturally homogeneous market with identical languages and preferences.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_ASIAN_POPULATION_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_401_332CEA"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_26606B5A", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"The source evidence is: second largest multicultural group in the United States; made up of three different subethnicities: single race, Black Hispanic, or Black mixed with another race (White or Native American) Which concrete detail contradicts this claim about black population: Black consumers share a single ancestry, identity, and purchasing pattern.", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:38.912Z'), rung:0, rationale:"Requires a concrete source detail that falsifies the stated assumption about black population.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_BLACK_POPULATION_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_402_9B9589"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_7F032D3F", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"Using the framework of marketing to hispanic, black, and asian consumers, how would you explain black population correctly, and which distinction does the flawed claim erase?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:38.912Z'), rung:1, rationale:"Re-establishes the relevant marketing relationship or classification. Evidence to use: second largest multicultural group in the United States; made up of three different subethnicities: single race, Black Hispanic, or Black mixed with another race (White or Native American)", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_BLACK_POPULATION_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_402_9B9589"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_C1A90A47", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"If you applied this claim about black population to a different product, customer group, or organization, what evidence would you check before accepting it, and what result would make you reject it?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:38.912Z'), rung:2, rationale:"Transfers the identified reasoning error to a new marketing decision while requiring a falsifiable check rather than copying the claim: Black consumers share a single ancestry, identity, and purchasing pattern.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_BLACK_POPULATION_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_402_9B9589"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_D84ACCEA", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"The source evidence is: a company’s approach to focusing decisions and execution from the perspective of the organization rather than the customers Which concrete detail contradicts this claim about company centric: A company-centric decision is necessarily based on direct evidence of customer needs.", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:38.912Z'), rung:0, rationale:"Requires a concrete source detail that falsifies the stated assumption about company centric.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_COMPANY_CENTRIC_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_403_769AE2"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_15200A22", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"Using the framework of diversity and inclusion marketing, how would you explain company centric correctly, and which distinction does the flawed claim erase?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:38.912Z'), rung:1, rationale:"Re-establishes the relevant marketing relationship or classification. Evidence to use: a company’s approach to focusing decisions and execution from the perspective of the organization rather than the customers", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_COMPANY_CENTRIC_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_403_769AE2"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_92DE6397", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"If you applied this claim about company centric to a different product, customer group, or organization, what 