e: a strategic approach that involves identifying different subsegments of the population—based on shared cultural and sociodemographic characteristics—and creating intentional marketing efforts to connect with these consumer groups", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_DIVERSITY_MARKETING_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_409_734E10"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_333243DA", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"If you applied this claim about diversity marketing to a different product, customer group, or organization, what evidence would you check before accepting it, and what result would make you reject it?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:38.912Z'), rung:2, rationale:"Transfers the identified reasoning error to a new marketing decision while requiring a falsifiable check rather than copying the claim: Changing the ethnic appearance of an advertisement fully addresses inclusion.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_DIVERSITY_MARKETING_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_409_734E10"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_EFA215BE", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"The source evidence is: the capability of identifying, accepting, and valuing the diverseness of consumers within a market and using this knowledge to tailor the marketing mix accordingly Which concrete detail contradicts this claim about diversity marketing intelligence (dmiq): Population labels alone provide sufficient knowledge to tailor marketing responsibly.", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:38.912Z'), rung:0, rationale:"Requires a concrete source detail that falsifies the stated assumption about diversity marketing intelligence (dmiq).", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_DIVERSITY_MARKETING_INTELLIGENCE_DMIQ_DIAGNOSTIC_CB00A1"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_9F107B49", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"Using the framework of diversity and inclusion marketing, how would you explain diversity marketing intelligence (dmiq) correctly, and which distinction does the flawed claim erase?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:38.912Z'), rung:1, rationale:"Re-establishes the relevant marketing relationship or classification. Evidence to use: the capability of identifying, accepting, and valuing the diverseness of consumers within a market and using this knowledge to tailor the marketing mix accordingly", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_DIVERSITY_MARKETING_INTELLIGENCE_DMIQ_DIAGNOSTIC_CB00A1"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_063B0C21", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"If you applied this claim about diversity marketing intelligence (dmiq) to a different product, customer group, or organization, what evidence would you check before accepting it, and what result would make you reject it?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:38.912Z'), rung:2, rationale:"Transfers the identified reasoning error to a new marketing decision while requiring a falsifiable check rather than copying the claim: Population labels alone provide sufficient knowledge to tailor marketing responsibly.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_DIVERSITY_MARKETING_INTELLIGENCE_DMIQ_DIAGNOSTIC_CB00A1"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_993CBA55", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"The source evidence is: sociodemographic category based on birth year clusters that includes Lost Generation (1883–1900), Greatest Generation (1901–1927), Traditionalist/Silent Generation (1928–1945), baby boomers (1946–1964), Generation X (1965–1980), millennials/Generation Y (1981–1996), Zoomers/ Generation Z (1997–2009), and Generation Alpha (2010–2024) Which concrete detail contradicts this claim about generational population: Birth-year cohorts determine every individual's attitudes and buying behavior.", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:38.912Z'), rung:0, rationale:"Requires a concrete source detail that falsifies the stated assumption about generational popula