oduct to protect a portfolio Which concrete detail contradicts this claim about divest: Divesting and reducing discretionary expenditure while continuing sales are the same action.", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:38.912Z'), rung:0, rationale:"Requires a concrete source detail that falsifies the stated assumption about divest.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_DIVEST_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_444_1A5D2E"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_4F1D3AD4", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"Using the framework of marketing strategies at each stage of the product life cycle, how would you explain divest correctly, and which distinction does the flawed claim erase?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:38.912Z'), rung:1, rationale:"Re-establishes the relevant marketing relationship or classification. Evidence to use: to sell a brand or discontinue a product to protect a portfolio", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_DIVEST_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_444_1A5D2E"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_8BA81C73", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"If you applied this claim about divest to a different product, customer group, or organization, what evidence would you check before accepting it, and what result would make you reject it?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:38.912Z'), rung:2, rationale:"Transfers the identified reasoning error to a new marketing decision while requiring a falsifiable check rather than copying the claim: Divesting and reducing discretionary expenditure while continuing sales are the same action.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_DIVEST_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_444_1A5D2E"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_002F2AC7", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"An item sells for 100 monetary units and has cost of goods sold of 60. What gross margin results before other expenses, and why is the denominator sales rather than cost?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:38.912Z'), rung:0, rationale:"Uses the stated numerical scenario or explicit source distinction to expose the specific mistaken denominator, classification, or interpretation.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_GROSS_PROFIT_MARGIN_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_445_8B5DB2"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_F554B301", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"Using the framework of forms of brand development, brand loyalty, and brand metrics, how would you explain gross profit margin correctly, and which distinction does the flawed claim erase?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:38.912Z'), rung:1, rationale:"Re-establishes the relevant marketing relationship or classification. Evidence to use: Revenue minus cost of goods sold, divided by revenue and expressed as a percentage. Gross profit precedes other operating expenses; it is not profit before all costs.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_GROSS_PROFIT_MARGIN_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_445_8B5DB2"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_658E35EF", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"If you applied this claim about gross profit margin to a different product, customer group, or organization, what evidence would you check before accepting it, and what result would make you reject it?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:38.912Z'), rung:2, rationale:"Transfers the identified reasoning error to a new marketing decision while requiring a falsifiable check rather than copying the claim: Gross margin deducts every operating expense and tax from revenue.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_GROSS_PROFIT_MARGIN_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_445_8B5DB2"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_4457CC6C", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"The source evidence is: part of the product life cycle characterized by increasing sales; stage when copycat brands may enter the market Which concrete detail contradicts this claim about growth stage: Sales