nd brand development, how would you explain national brands correctly, and which distinction does the flawed claim erase?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.073Z'), rung:1, rationale:"Re-establishes the relevant marketing relationship or classification. Evidence to use: name brands that sell a product or service under its corporate name and identity", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_NATIONAL_BRANDS_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_456_1E2B38"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_499E8BB3", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"If you applied this claim about national brands to a different product, customer group, or organization, what evidence would you check before accepting it, and what result would make you reject it?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.073Z'), rung:2, rationale:"Transfers the identified reasoning error to a new marketing decision while requiring a falsifiable check rather than copying the claim: A national brand is the retailer's own private label.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_NATIONAL_BRANDS_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_456_1E2B38"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_5C2EC0A3", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"A constructed business has revenue of 1,000 and net profit of 100 after expenses. What is its net margin, and why does the revenue figure alone not reveal profitability?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.073Z'), rung:0, rationale:"Uses the stated numerical scenario or explicit source distinction to expose the specific mistaken denominator, classification, or interpretation.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_NET_PROFIT_MARGIN_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_457_6C74FD"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_117DA081", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"Using the framework of forms of brand development, brand loyalty, and brand metrics, how would you explain net profit margin correctly, and which distinction does the flawed claim erase?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.073Z'), rung:1, rationale:"Re-establishes the relevant marketing relationship or classification. Evidence to use: Net profit after relevant expenses divided by revenue, expressed as a percentage; distinguish this from gross profit margin, which subtracts cost of goods sold before other expenses.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_NET_PROFIT_MARGIN_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_457_6C74FD"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_1CAB0B91", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"If you applied this claim about net profit margin to a different product, customer group, or organization, what evidence would you check before accepting it, and what result would make you reject it?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.073Z'), rung:2, rationale:"Transfers the identified reasoning error to a new marketing decision while requiring a falsifiable check rather than copying the claim: Net margin is revenue before any costs are deducted.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_NET_PROFIT_MARGIN_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_457_6C74FD"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_7943F61D", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"The source evidence is: an entirely different brand entity from a parent company Which concrete detail contradicts this claim about new brands: A new brand is merely a new package size under the same existing name.", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.073Z'), rung:0, rationale:"Requires a concrete source detail that falsifies the stated assumption about new brands.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_NEW_BRANDS_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_458_F15AFB"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_58430228", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"Using the framework of forms of brand development, brand loyalty, and brand metrics, how would you explain new brands correctly, and which distinction does the flawed claim erase?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.