_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"If you applied this claim about return on ad spend (roas) to a different product, customer group, or organization, what evidence would you check before accepting it, and what result would make you reject it?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.392Z'), rung:2, rationale:"Transfers the identified reasoning error to a new marketing decision while requiring a falsifiable check rather than copying the claim: ROAS measures net profit after every business cost.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_RETURN_ON_AD_SPEND_ROAS_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_054826"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_C29973DC", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"The source evidence is: advertising budget strategy that focuses on every dollar spent on advertising; a return of that dollar—plus some—is expected Which concrete detail contradicts this claim about return-on-investment (roi) approach: Advertising return can be assessed without considering incremental outcomes or cost.", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.392Z'), rung:0, rationale:"Requires a concrete source detail that falsifies the stated assumption about return-on-investment (roi) approach.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_RETURN_ON_INVESTMENT_ROI_APPROACH_DIAGNOSTIC_MIS_AB7EA5"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_88576340", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"Using the framework of major decisions in developing an advertising plan, how would you explain return-on-investment (roi) approach correctly, and which distinction does the flawed claim erase?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.392Z'), rung:1, rationale:"Re-establishes the relevant marketing relationship or classification. Evidence to use: advertising budget strategy that focuses on every dollar spent on advertising; a return of that dollar—plus some—is expected", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_RETURN_ON_INVESTMENT_ROI_APPROACH_DIAGNOSTIC_MIS_AB7EA5"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_C73CE1C2", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"If you applied this claim about return-on-investment (roi) approach to a different product, customer group, or organization, what evidence would you check before accepting it, and what result would make you reject it?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.392Z'), rung:2, rationale:"Transfers the identified reasoning error to a new marketing decision while requiring a falsifiable check rather than copying the claim: Advertising return can be assessed without considering incremental outcomes or cost.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_RETURN_ON_INVESTMENT_ROI_APPROACH_DIAGNOSTIC_MIS_AB7EA5"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_6945A6F3", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"The source evidence is: a type of posttest in advertising that determines how many sales will be made based on a test market Which concrete detail contradicts this claim about sales test: Sales in one test market necessarily predict all markets without qualification.", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.392Z'), rung:0, rationale:"Requires a concrete source detail that falsifies the stated assumption about sales test.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_SALES_TEST_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_681_818389"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_9163C410", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"Using the framework of major decisions in developing an advertising plan, how would you explain sales test correctly, and which distinction does the flawed claim erase?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.392Z'), rung:1, rationale:"Re-establishes the relevant marketing relationship or classification. Evidence to use: a type of posttest in advertising that determines how many sales will be made based on a test market", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_SALES_TEST_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_681_818389"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_E79061CA", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"If you applied this claim about sales test to a different product, customer group, or organization, what evidence would you check before accepting it, and what result would make you reject it?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.392Z'), rung:2, rationale:"Transfers the identified reasoning error to a new marketing decision while requiring a falsifiable check rather than copying the claim: Sales in one test market necessarily predict all markets without qualification.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_SALES_TEST_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_681_818389"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_0B55A817", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"The source evidence is: a form of advertising pretest in which the audience is shown advertisements—usually television ads—in the context that they would be shown to the entire market Which concrete detail contradicts this claim about theater tests: Viewing an advertisement in a controlled theater perfectly duplicates everyday exposure.", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.392Z'), rung:0, rationale:"Requires a concrete source detail that falsifies the stated assumption about theater tests.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_THEATER_TESTS_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_682_82B6C8"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_6130421D", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"Using the framework of major decisions in developing an advertising plan, how would you explain theater tests correctly, and which distinction does the flawed claim erase?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.392Z'), rung:1, rationale:"Re-establishes the relevant marketing relationship or classification. Evidence to use: a form of advertising pretest in which the audience is shown advertisements—usually television ads—in the context that they would be shown to the entire market", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_THEAT