CCBB5B"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_E21A58B4", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"A constructed campaign spends 500 monetary units on 100 clicks that produce 10 purchases. What is CPC, and why is it different from cost per purchase?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.392Z'), rung:0, rationale:"Uses the stated numerical scenario or explicit source distinction to expose the specific mistaken denominator, classification, or interpretation.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_COST_PER_CLICK_CPC_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_736_0397FC"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_0D20B453", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"Using the framework of metrics used to evaluate the success of online marketing, how would you explain cost per click (cpc) correctly, and which distinction does the flawed claim erase?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.392Z'), rung:1, rationale:"Re-establishes the relevant marketing relationship or classification. Evidence to use: the cost companies pay search engines for each click that a search advertisement receives, which is based on the keywords a company bids on", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_COST_PER_CLICK_CPC_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_736_0397FC"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_377F3C69", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"If you applied this claim about cost per click (cpc) to a different product, customer group, or organization, what evidence would you check before accepting it, and what result would make you reject it?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.392Z'), rung:2, rationale:"Transfers the identified reasoning error to a new marketing decision while requiring a falsifiable check rather than copying the claim: CPC measures the cost of a confirmed customer purchase.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_COST_PER_CLICK_CPC_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_736_0397FC"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_2B249E42", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac