ips.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_EMAIL_MARKETING_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_740_209210"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_D6BDCF27", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"The source evidence is: when users see an online ad Which concrete detail contradicts this claim about impression: An impression proves the user clicked and understood the advertisement.", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.392Z'), rung:0, rationale:"Requires a concrete source detail that falsifies the stated assumption about impression.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_IMPRESSION_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_741_C41626"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_685BCCC9", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"Using the framework of metrics used to evaluate the success of online marketing, how would you explain impression correctly, and which distinction does the flawed claim erase?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.392Z'), rung:1, rationale:"Re-establishes the relevant marketing relationship or classification. Evidence to use: when users see an online ad", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_IMPRESSION_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_741_C41626"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_5412F51C", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"If you applied this claim about impression to a different product, customer group, or organization, what evidence would you check before accepting it, and what result would make you reject it?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.392Z'), rung:2, rationale:"Transfers the identified reasoning error to a new marketing decision while requiring a falsifiable check rather than copying the claim: An impression proves the user clicked and understood the advertisement.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_IMPRESSION_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_741_C41626"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_630983A0", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"The source evidence is: 