m about mobile marketing to a different product, customer group, or organization, what evidence would you check before accepting it, and what result would make you reject it?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.392Z'), rung:2, rationale:"Transfers the identified reasoning error to a new marketing decision while requiring a falsifiable check rather than copying the claim: A desktop campaign can always be copied unchanged onto a small screen.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_MOBILE_MARKETING_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_744_2B500B"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_D3C9F519", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"The source evidence is: emails whose images, text, and links display in a way that is easy to read when accessed via a mobile device Which concrete detail contradicts this claim about mobile-friendly emails: Shrinking desktop text is sufficient even if links and layout become unusable.", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.392Z'), rung:0, rationale:"Requires a concrete source detail that falsifies the stated assumption about mobile-friendly emails.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_MOBILE_FRIENDLY_EMAILS_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION__EEEA9C"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_8058F8C3", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"Using the framework of social media and mobile marketing, how would you explain mobile-friendly emails correctly, and which distinction does the flawed claim erase?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.392Z'), rung:1, rationale:"Re-establishes the relevant marketing relationship or classification. Evidence to use: emails whose images, text, and links display in a way that is easy to read when accessed via a mobile device", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_MOBILE_FRIENDLY_EMAILS_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION__EEEA9C"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_AB51D6A1", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"If you applied this claim about mobile-friendly emails to a different product, customer group, or organization, what evidence would you check before accepting it, and what result would make you reject it?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.392Z'), rung:2, rationale:"Transfers the identified reasoning error to a new marketing decision while requiring a falsifiable check rather than copying the claim: Shrinking desktop text is sufficient even if links and layout become unusable.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_MOBILE_FRIENDLY_EMAILS_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION__EEEA9C"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_7880700D", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"The source evidence is: people who are first visiting your website, also known as new users Which concrete detail contradicts this claim about new visitors: A newly recognized browser identifier necessarily represents a person who has never encountered the brand.", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.392Z'), rung:0, rationale:"Requires a concrete source detail that falsifies the stated assumption about new visitors.", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_NEW_VISITORS_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_746_4CB1DF"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_ABE67270", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"Using the framework of metrics used to evaluate the success of online marketing, how would you explain new visitors correctly, and which distinction does the flawed claim erase?", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:39.392Z'), rung:1, rationale:"Re-establishes the relevant marketing relationship or classification. Evidence to use: people who are first visiting your website, also known as new users", status:"approved", misconception_id:"MISC_NEW_VISITORS_DIAGNOSTIC_MISCONCEPTION_746_4CB1DF"}}, {probe_id:"PROBE_7228CB3A", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", probe_text:"If you applied this claim about new visitors to a different product, customer group, or organization, what evidence would 