s to caste, religious, and linguistic diversity.", label:"Evaluating India's Constitutional Design", canonical_key:"EVALUATING_INDIA_S_CONSTITUTIONAL_DESIGN", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"CON_COMPARING_DEVELOPMENT_MODELS_IN_INDIA_5E2CAB", kc_id:"CON_COMPARING_DEVELOPMENT_MODELS_IN_INDIA_5E2CAB", properties:{course_id:"2bf5b7c4-01ee-4ee5-9c8b-f2066289192a", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:01:51.748Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"relationship", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:01:51.748Z'), definition:"Analyzing the evolution from Nehruvian state-led industrialization through the License Raj to 1991 liberalization, evaluating tradeoffs between equity and growth strategies.", label:"Comparing Development Models in India", canonical_key:"COMPARING_DEVELOPMENT_MODELS_IN_INDIA", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"CON_ANALYZING_LINGUISTIC_FEDERALISM_3571AA", kc_id:"CON_ANALYZING_LINGUISTIC_FEDERALISM_3571AA", properties:{course_id:"2bf5b7c4-01ee-4ee5-9c8b-f2066289192a", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:01:51.755Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:01:51.755Z'), definition:"Evaluating how linguistic state reorganization both accommodated diversity and created new tensions, comparing with other multilingual nations' strategies.", label:"Analyzing Linguistic Federalism", canonical_key:"ANALYZING_LINGUISTIC_FEDERALISM", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"CON_ANALYZING_HARAPPAN_ARCHAEOLOGICAL_EVIDENCE_EE9736", kc_id:"CON_ANALYZING_HARAPPAN_ARCHAEOLOGICAL_EVIDENCE_EE9736", properties:{course_id:"2bf5b7c4-01ee-4ee5-9c8b-f2066289192a", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:01:51.541Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", created_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:01:51.541Z'), definition:"Evaluating archaeological artifacts including seals, pottery, city layouts, and trade goods to reconstruct Harappan society, governance, and commercial net