ey Terms, printed page 120; related section 3.1.", label:"Analyze buyer’s black box", canonical_key:"analyze_buyer_s_black_box", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"79aaa815-d5ec-591c-a85e-38e392c735a3", kc_id:"79aaa815-d5ec-591c-a85e-38e392c735a3", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"threshold", definition:"Analyze cognitive dissonance: the mental conflict that occurs when a person’s behaviors and beliefs do not align; also referred to as buyer’s remorse Source: chapter 3 Key Terms, printed page 120; related section 3.3.", label:"Analyze cognitive dissonance", canonical_key:"analyze_cognitive_dissonance", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"8b44b484-60d8-500a-8cda-34ef2c1ded62", kc_id:"8b44b484-60d8-500a-8cda-34ef2c1ded62", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"process", definition:"Explain complex buying behavior: the consumer buying behavior that occurs when the consumer is highly involved with the purchase and perceives significant differences between brands Source: chapter 3 Key Terms, printed page 120; related section 3.1.", label:"Explain complex buying behavior", canonical_key:"explain_complex_buying_behavior", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"c3c50dfc-192c-5c25-b105-17ce522ce6dc", kc_id:"c3c50dfc-192c-5c25-b105-17ce522ce6dc", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"process", definition:"Explain consumer buying behavior: the actions taken by consumers before buying a product or service Source: chapter 3 Key Terms, printed page 120; related section 3.1.", label:"Explain consumer buying behavior", canonical_key:"explain_consumer_buying_behavior", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"fbc8550e-b99b-5ae2-bca9-c95a23e03b19", kc_id:"fbc8550e-b99b-5ae2-bca9-c95a23e03b19", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"process", definition:"Explain consumer decision process: the process through which consumers become aware of and identify their needs, collect information on how to best solve those needs, evaluate alternative options, make a purchasing decision, and evaluate their purchase Source: chapter 3 Key Terms, printed page 120; related section 3.3.", label:"Explain consumer decision process", canonical_key:"explain_consumer_decision_process", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"d8f115fc-e821-5bbe-b0a9-6f57772e7ed8", kc_id:"d8f115fc-e821-5bbe-b0a9-6f57772e7ed8", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"entity", definition:"Explain consumer market: a market where consumers purchase products and/or services for consumption Source: chapter 3 Key Terms, printed page 120; related section 3.2.", label:"Explain consumer market", canonical_key:"explain_consumer_market", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"87a0d2af-90e0-5286-a2ff-3b484dc30fc0", kc_id:"87a0d2af-90e0-5286-a2ff-3b484dc30fc0", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"domain", definition:"Explain cultural factors: a set of values or ideologies of a particular community or group of individuals that include culture, subcultures, social class, and gender Source: chapter 3 Key Terms, printed page 120; related section 3.2.", label:"Explain cultural factors", canonical_key:"explain_cultural_factors", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"295336ee-9e18-5baf-93d9-b03a0b24becb", kc_id:"295336ee-9e18-5baf-93d9-b03a0b24becb", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"domain", definition:"Explain culture: the pattern of learned and shared behavior and beliefs of a particular social, ethnic, or age group Source: chapter 3 Key Terms, printed page 120; related section 3.2.", label:"Explain culture", canonical_key:"explain_culture", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"c0aeeb45-ac70-5729-8aa6-376052533df0", kc_id:"c0aeeb45-ac70-5729-8aa6-376052533df0", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"threshold", definition:"Analyze dissonance-reducing buying behavior: any activity aimed at decreasing the tension or feelings of discomfort and unease that accompany an unfamiliar purchase Source: chapter 3 Key Terms, printed page 120; related section 3.1.", label:"Analyze dissonance-reducing buying behavior", canonical_key:"analyze_dissonance_reducing_buying_behavior", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"14123556-8489-5f17-bd96-1b3bad69da5f", kc_id:"14123556-8489-5f17-bd96-1b3bad69da5f", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"domain", definition:"Explain economic situation: a measure of a consumer’s income and financial situation Source: chapter 3 Key Terms, printed page 120; related section 3.2.", label:"Explain economic situation", canonical_key:"explain_economic_situation", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"20116b3b-692b-5563-9f22-b2f82ecec66d", kc_id:"20116b3b-692b-5563-9f22-b2f82ecec66d", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"domain", definition:"Explain environmental factors: factors such as music, lighting, ambient noise, and smell that can either discourage or encourage a consumer’s purchase decision Source: chapter 3 Key Terms, printed page 120; related section 3.2.", label:"Explain environmental factors", canonical_key:"explain_environmental_factors", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"da857466-7bed-57c9-b138-7e440a4c522f", kc_id:"da857466-7bed-57c9-b138-7e440a4c522f", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"domain", definition:"Explain family: a group of persons united by ties of marriage, blood, or adoption, or those who live in the same household Source: chapter 3 Key Terms, printed page 120; related section 3.2.", label:"Explain family", canonical_key:"explain_family", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"a045782c-d386-5e80-9c8d-3f7bd30815f9", kc_id:"a045782c-d386-5e80-9c8d-3f7bd30815f9", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"domain", definition:"Explain gender: the socially constructed roles, behaviors, and norms of individuals, which vary between societies and over time Source: chapter 3 Key Terms, printed page 120; related section 3.2.", label:"Explain gender", canonical_key:"explain_gender", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"39b38f56-4d73-5857-a5da-b0d6823ed4c3", kc_id:"39b38f56-4d73-5857-a5da-b0d6823ed4c3", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"process", definition:"Explain habitual buying behavior: consumer buying decisions made out of “habit” and without much deliberation or product comparison Source: chapter 3 Key Terms, printed page 120; related section 3.1.", label:"Explain habitual buying behavior", canonical_key:"explain_habitual_buying_behavior", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"2d385689-6047-577f-adaa-7355c9ee90bc", kc_id:"2d385689-6047-577f-adaa-7355c9ee90bc", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"domain", definition:"Explain heuristics: mental shortcuts that allow people to solve problems and make judgments quickly and efficiently Source: chapter 3 Key Terms, printed page 120; related section 3.3.", label:"Explain heuristics", canonical_key:"explain_heuristics", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"01d3299a-7388-5cea-b55d-1b7c3b28b2b6", kc_id:"01d3299a-7388-5cea-b55d-1b7c3b28b2b6", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"process", definition:"Explain learning: the acquisition of knowledge or skills through experience, study, or being taught Source: chapter 3 Key Terms, printed page 120; related section 3.2.", label:"Explain learning", canonical_key:"explain_learning", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"0df32088-b42d-5ae9-9556-31a701c55534", kc_id:"0df32088-b42d-5ae9-9556-31a701c55534", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"domain", definition:"Explain life cycle stages: various stages in a human’s life, including fetus, baby, childhood, adolescence, adulthood, and elderly Source: chapter 3 Key Terms, printed page 120; related section 3.2.", label:"Explain life cycle stages", canonical_key:"explain_life_cycle_stages", status:"approved"}}] AS row
