fidentiality: a situation where the researcher promises to hold private information but discloses it in an unethical manner without permission Source: chapter 6 Key Terms, printed page 219; related section 6.4.", label:"Evaluate breach of confidentiality", canonical_key:"evaluate_breach_of_confidentiality", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"e1396447-9f0b-5885-ae49-a9fdadd1413c", kc_id:"e1396447-9f0b-5885-ae49-a9fdadd1413c", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"apply", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Apply causal research: studies that define a cause-and-effect relationship between two factors Source: chapter 6 Key Terms, printed page 219; related section 6.3.", label:"Apply causal research", canonical_key:"apply_causal_research", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"a8adbe92-5f66-5f10-bdf1-ade258eadc20", kc_id:"a8adbe92-5f66-5f10-bdf1-ade258eadc20", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"domain", definition:"Explain census: when all potential target population members are included in the research Source: chapter 6 Key Terms, printed page 219; related section 6.3.", label:"Explain census", canonical_key:"explain_census", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"b49ba881-fdec-5148-aa65-f840bca45843", kc_id:"b49ba881-fdec-5148-aa65-f840bca45843", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"domain", definition:"Explain competitive intelligence: a collection of information about competitors from the marketplace Source: chapter 6 Key Terms, printed page 219; related section 6.2.", label:"Explain competitive intelligence", canonical_key:"explain_competitive_intelligence", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"e849aa70-eefc-5d29-bb6c-14f2a00d196d", kc_id:"e849aa70-eefc-5d29-bb6c-14f2a00d196d", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"domain", definition:"Evaluate confidential data: data that is tied back to a respondent, but the respondent’s personal information is not shared Source: chapter 6 Key Terms, printed page 219; related section 6.4.", label:"Evaluate confidential data", canonical_key:"evaluate_confidential_data", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"96d0e55d-90ac-586f-8a04-5cd54bf6341c", kc_id:"96d0e55d-90ac-586f-8a04-5cd54bf6341c", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"apply", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Apply convenience sample: a nonprobability sample type where potential respondents to the research are selected by convenience rather than through any scientific method Source: chapter 6 Key Terms, printed page 219; related section 6.3.", label:"Apply convenience sample", canonical_key:"apply_convenience_sample", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"e14888b8-719a-5d6c-a50e-39621476f45b", kc_id:"e14888b8-719a-5d6c-a50e-39621476f45b", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"domain", definition:"Explain cross tabulation: an analysis of two variables and the frequency of each answer in relation to the other variable Source: chapter 6 Key Terms, printed page 219; related section 6.3.", label:"Explain cross tabulation", canonical_key:"explain_cross_tabulation", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"c686c291-815d-555c-8041-479db161e912", kc_id:"c686c291-815d-555c-8041-479db161e912", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"relationship", definition:"Analyze customer acquisition cost: the total expenses a company spends to gain a new customer Source: chapter 6 Key Terms, printed page 219; related section 6.3.", label:"Analyze customer acquisition cost", canonical_key:"analyze_customer_acquisition_cost", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"9ecd3305-6c94-5ea0-9fbc-e2310fea26b3", kc_id:"9ecd3305-6c94-5ea0-9fbc-e2310fea26b3", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"apply", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Apply customer effort score: a survey used to measure ease of service experience with an organization Source: chapter 6 Key Terms, printed page 219; related section 6.3.", label:"Apply customer effort score", canonical_key:"apply_customer_effort_score", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"48bc83bd-f69c-5f1a-be2c-2e538a8a585c", kc_id:"48bc83bd-f69c-5f1a-be2c-2e538a8a585c", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"apply", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Apply customer satisfaction score: A measure of how satisfied customers are with a product, brand, or service, described as CSAT in section 6.3. Source inconsistency: the chapter glossary mistakenly repeats the customer effort score definition; this node follows the substantive section. Source: chapter 6 Key Terms, printed page 219; related section 6.3.", label:"Apply customer satisfaction score", canonical_key:"apply_customer_satisfaction_score", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"7def54e7-d7bc-5859-bc60-227239a381b9", kc_id:"7def54e7-d7bc-5859-bc60-227239a381b9", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"apply", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Apply data analysis: the distillation of information into a more understandable and actionable format Source: chapter 6 Key Terms, printed page 219; related section 6.3.", label:"Apply data analysis", canonical_key:"apply_data_analysis", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"2ea1add6-cd47-571d-8785-7e4e66c7efcd", kc_id:"2ea1add6-cd47-571d-8785-7e4e66c7efcd", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"process", definition:"Explain data collection: systematic gathering of information that addresses an identified problem Source: chapter 6 Key Terms, printed page 219; related section 6.1.", label:"Explain data collection", canonical_key:"explain_data_collection", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"82672235-cfe4-5c05-b8c2-e95b2da3f5b0", kc_id:"82672235-cfe4-5c05-b8c2-e95b2da3f5b0", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"domain", definition:"Explain database: a collection of related data Source: chapter 6 Key Terms, printed page 219; related section 6.2.", label:"Explain database", canonical_key:"explain_database", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"f192d74d-2a93-5a89-8b83-51d7c15c95ac", kc_id:"f192d74d-2a93-5a89-8b83-51d7c15c95ac", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"apply", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Apply descriptive research: data collected to describe the situation in the market and help define an opinion, attitude, or behavior Source: chapter 6 Key Terms, printed page 219; related section 6.3.", label:"Apply descriptive research", canonical_key:"apply_descriptive_research", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"32198b52-e873-5f7f-85bb-c89041cda47f", kc_id:"32198b52-e873-5f7f-85bb-c89041cda47f", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"apply", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Apply electronic surveys: surveys sent through digital means to respondents; respondents also reply to the survey digitally Source: chapter 6 Key Terms, printed page 219; related section 6.3.", label:"Apply electronic surveys", canonical_key:"apply_electronic_surveys", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"fe1efb40-7a76-55c4-961e-04d1d8761447", kc_id:"fe1efb40-7a76-55c4-961e-04d1d8761447", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"apply", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Apply ethnographic research: method of collecting data that is conducted by observing people’s natural behavior Source: chapter 6 Key Terms, printed page 219; related section 6.3.", label:"Apply ethnographic research", canonical_key:"apply_ethnographic_research", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"6a344f1e-a4a8-5345-848a-027ca958a2f6", kc_id:"6a344f1e-a4a8-5345-848a-027ca958a2f6", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"apply", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Apply experimental research: studies that define a cause-and-effect relationship between two factors Source: chapter 6 Key Terms, printed page 219; related section 6.3.", label:"Apply experimental research", canonical_key:"apply_experimental_research", status:"approved"}}] AS row
