e: a sample in which everyone has a known chance of being included in the research Source: chapter 6 Key Terms, printed page 219; related section 6.3.", label:"Apply probability sample", canonical_key:"apply_probability_sample", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"7202cdf7-c0de-5e1c-b04a-9fc0da613a1e", kc_id:"7202cdf7-c0de-5e1c-b04a-9fc0da613a1e", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"domain", definition:"Explain problem definition: the realization that there is an issue that needs to be addressed Source: chapter 6 Key Terms, printed page 219; related section 6.3.", label:"Explain problem definition", canonical_key:"explain_problem_definition", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"93159869-691c-5835-80db-281c9afa498a", kc_id:"93159869-691c-5835-80db-281c9afa498a", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"domain", definition:"Explain qualitative data: data that cannot be distilled into number of responses, such as responses to an interview Source: chapter 6 Key Terms, printed page 219; related section 6.3.", label:"Explain qualitative data", canonical_key:"explain_qualitative_data", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"68654650-018c-5a28-b17f-41fe3d18fb07", kc_id:"68654650-018c-5a28-b17f-41fe3d18fb07", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"apply", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.476Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Apply qualitative research: data shared through words, descriptions, and open-ended comments Source: chapter 6 Key Terms, printed page 219; related section 6.3.", label:"Apply qualitative research", canonical_key:"apply_qualitative_research", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"239c5bd1-f5d7-584c-9e38-8f483dd24e21", kc_id:"23