rgy: the extent to which a new product is built on the firm’s existing technological resources Source: chapter 10 Key Terms, printed page 366; related section 10.4.", label:"Analyze technological synergy", canonical_key:"analyze_technological_synergy", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"1b612659-f55b-555b-8a1f-6ee18cd16571", kc_id:"1b612659-f55b-555b-8a1f-6ee18cd16571", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"apply", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Apply test-marketing: the seventh step in the new product development process, in which a product concept is test-marketed to determine its viability before launch to market Source: chapter 10 Key Terms, printed page 366; related section 10.2.", label:"Apply test-marketing", canonical_key:"apply_test_marketing", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"0db5a43a-cdec-5b86-9618-1e1d30757c50", kc_id:"0db5a43a-cdec-5b86-9618-1e1d30757c50", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"entity", definition:"Explain trademarks: words or symbols legally registered or established by use as representing a company or product Source: chapter 10 Key Terms, printed page 366; related section 10.6.", label:"Explain trademarks", canonical_key:"explain_trademarks", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"1e44d76a-b1c7-59ec-801a-8a213ba91cb5", kc_id:"1e44d76a-b1c7-59ec-801a-8a213ba91cb5", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"domain", definition:"Explain assurance: in terms of the RATER model, the degree to which an organization inspires trust in its customers Source: chapter 11 Key Terms, printed page 398; related section 11.3.", label:"Explain assurance", canonical_key:"explain_assurance", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"88bba3d7-fdfc-59c7-841a-0a6e205b6b82", kc_id:"88bba3d7-fdfc-59c7-841a-0a6e205b6b82", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"relationship", definition:"Analyze communication gap: in the Gap Model of Service Quality, the variance between what is communicated to the customer and their actual experience Source: chapter 11 Key Terms, printed page 398; related section 11.3.", label:"Analyze communication gap", canonical_key:"analyze_communication_gap", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"1fa9d207-ed19-54d1-a9fa-4187474fd048", kc_id:"1fa9d207-ed19-54d1-a9fa-4187474fd048", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"relationship", definition:"Analyze customer gap: in the Gap Model of Service Quality, the variance between the customer’s expectations and their perception of the service Source: chapter 11 Key Terms, printed page 398; related section 11.3.", label:"Analyze customer gap", canonical_key:"analyze_customer_gap", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"6d1a64c7-025f-5656-8b4b-55df38a3bd6f", kc_id:"6d1a64c7-025f-5656-8b4b-55df38a3bd6f", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"relationship", definition:"Analyze customer loyalty: an ongoing positive relationship between a customer and a business that drives repeat purchases Source: chapter 11 Key Terms, printed page 398; related section 11.2.", label:"Analyze customer loyalty", canonical_key:"analyze_customer_loyalty", status:"approved"}}] AS row
