ey Terms, printed page 398; related section 11.2.", label:"Explain external service marketing", canonical_key:"explain_external_service_marketing", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"f03a9033-8e76-5f48-bc17-90d8bbf7d8ab", kc_id:"f03a9033-8e76-5f48-bc17-90d8bbf7d8ab", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"relationship", definition:"Analyze external value proposition: the value companies promise to deliver to customers post-purchase Source: chapter 11 Key Terms, printed page 398; related section 11.2.", label:"Analyze external value proposition", canonical_key:"analyze_external_value_proposition", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"50c02a9d-876f-59bc-aec7-f7719f1493be", kc_id:"50c02a9d-876f-59bc-aec7-f7719f1493be", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"apply", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Apply GAP Model of Service Quality: theoretical marketing model that helps to identify the gaps between the perceived service and the expected service Source: chapter 11 Key Terms, printed page 398; related section 11.3.", label:"Apply GAP Model of Service Quality", canonical_key:"apply_gap_model_of_service_quality", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"2c52a8a8-3b44-5e56-b1a3-61d5e2d0d995", kc_id:"2c52a8a8-3b44-5e56-b1a3-61d5e2d0d995", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"process", definition:"Explain information processing: intangible actions directed at a customer’s assets, such as insurance or consulting Source: chapter 11 Key Terms, printed page 398; related section 11.1.", label:"Explain information processing", canonical_key:"explain_information_processing", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"0bc57a05-9c1e-5ed1-944e-10b36b66c394", kc_id:"0bc57a05-9c1e-5ed1-944e-10b36b66c394", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"domain", definition:"Explain intangible: unable to be seen, tasted, felt, smelled, or heard Source: chapter 11 Key Terms, printed page 398; related section 11.1.", label:"Explain intangible", canonical_key:"explain_intangible", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"e09b8279-5ab8-5f82-be60-287d5a48816e", kc_id:"e09b8279-5ab8-5f82-be60-287d5a48816e", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"process", definition:"Explain interactive service marketing: The communication and direct interaction between the service provider and customer during the service encounter. Source: chapter 11 Key Terms, printed page 398; related section 11.2.", label:"Explain interactive service marketing", canonical_key:"explain_interactive_service_marketing", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"4fb13079-9c47-53f5-8eab-3f9eb5323e97", kc_id:"4fb13079-9c47-53f5-8eab-3f9eb5323e97", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"process", definition:"Explain internal service marketing: satisfying employees to motivate them to work as a team to satisfy customers Source: chapter 11 Key Terms, printed page 398; related section 11.2.", label:"Explain internal service marketing", canonical_key:"explain_internal_service_marketing", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"fd665397-d4c5-58ae-86fb-30c55427f764", kc_id:"fd665397-d4c5-58ae-86fb-30c55427f764", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"domain", definition:"Explain internal service quality: the perceived level of satisfaction an employee experiences with services offered by internal service providers Source: chapter 11 Key Terms, printed page 398; related section 11.2.", label:"Explain internal service quality", canonical_key:"explain_internal_service_quality", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"c05a4c86-9b4e-58b3-b9ed-847045be61e7", kc_id:"c05a4c86-9b4e-58b3-b9ed-847045be61e7", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"relationship", definition:"Analyze knowledge gap: in the GAP Model of Service Quality, the difference between what customers expect and what managers think they expect Source: chapter 11 Key Terms, printed page 398; related section 11.3.", label:"Analyze knowledge gap", canonical_key:"analyze_knowledge_gap", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"5a578e73-b744-5604-b089-c8f4850b9ea5", kc_id:"5a578e73-b744-5604-b089-c8f4850b9ea5", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"process", definition:"Explain mental stimulus processing: situation in which the services interact with the customer’s mind rather than the body Source: chapter 11 Key Terms, printed page 398; related section 11.1.", label:"Explain mental stimulus processing", canonical_key:"explain_mental_stimulus_processing", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"a173b1b2-106f-55fa-b445-42896e05e583", kc_id:"a173b1b2-106f-55fa-b445-42896e05e583", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"process", definition:"Explain people processing: services in which the customer is the direct recipient of the service and production and consumption are simultaneous Source: chapter 11 Key Terms, printed page 398; related section 11.1.", label:"Explain people processing", canonical_key:"explain_people_processing", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"38337339-44e9-506f-b15c-0e5f9dc76df1", kc_id:"38337339-44e9-506f-b15c-0e5f9dc76df1", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"domain", definition:"Explain people-based services: tasks in which people, rather than equipment or machinery, play a major role in the delivery of the service Source: chapter 11 Key Terms, printed page 398; related section 11.1.", label:"Explain people-based services", canonical_key:"explain_people_based_services", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"6f826014-bac8-508b-a3e7-b055f8e01a0f", kc_id:"6f826014-bac8-508b-a3e7-b055f8e01a0f", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"relationship", definition:"Analyze policy gap: in the GAP Model of Service Quality, the difference between managers understanding customer needs and being able to turn that into service delivery practices Source: chapter 11 Key Terms, printed page 398; related section 11.3.", label:"Analyze policy gap", canonical_key:"analyze_policy_gap", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"9f59555c-d74e-54e5-8ccc-3bb59d6b6fe9", kc_id:"9f59555c-d74e-54e5-8ccc-3bb59d6b6fe9", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"process", definition:"Explain possession processing: services in which the service is directed toward the customer’s physical possessions Source: chapter 11 Key Terms, printed page 398; related section 11.1.", label:"Explain possession processing", canonical_key:"explain_possession_processing", status:"approved"}}] AS row
