c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"apply", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Divide period revenue by the appropriate customer count, maintain a consistent period, and compare segments without treating revenue as profit. Source: section 2.4, printed page 72.", label:"Calculate average revenue per customer", canonical_key:"calculate_average_revenue_per_customer", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"47a29c80-a8c7-5c11-ad23-491a0a76bedd", kc_id:"47a29c80-a8c7-5c11-ad23-491a0a76bedd", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"relationship", definition:"Separate additional sales associated with an initiative from total sales and consider the comparison baseline. Source: section 2.4, printed page 72.", label:"Interpret incremental sales revenue", canonical_key:"interpret_incremental_sales_revenue", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"a0331fe5-ee58-5787-8709-b8a7a5076239", kc_id:"a0331fe5-ee58-5787-8709-b8a7a5076239", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"apply", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Distinguish the firm's share of category sales from its share relative to a leading competitor, specifying units or revenue and market boundaries. Source: section 2.4, printed page 72.", label:"Calculate market share and relative market share", canonical_key:"calculate_market_share_and_relative_market_share", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"15fcfa76-e7b2-5dc8-a686-5b5cfb088d03", kc_id:"15fcfa76-e7b2-5dc8-a686-5b5cfb088d03", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"apply", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Use a defined customer cohort and period to assess repeat relationships rather than counting newly acquired customers as retained customers. Source: section 2.4, printed page 72.", label:"Measure customer retention rates", canonical_key:"measure_customer_retention_rates", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"ac40ae9e-7e7e-570f-85a1-7dc22a4f06a7", kc_id:"ac40ae9e-7e7e-570f-85a1-7dc22a4f06a7", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Distinguish how many support cases are resolved from how long resolution takes, and consider service quality alongside speed. Source: section 2.4, printed page 72.", label:"Evaluate customer resolution rate and time", canonical_key:"evaluate_customer_resolution_rate_and_time", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"7e0796da-a0c4-5d00-8934-ebeb71dc67ab", kc_id:"7e0796da-a0c4-5d00-8934-ebeb71dc67ab", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Use the textbook's worked segment comparison to connect customer profit per period, retention duration, and acquisition investment, while distinguishing modeled estimates from realized cash flows. Source: section 2.4, printed page 72.", label:"Compare acquisition cost with customer lifetime value", canonical_key:"compare_acquisition_cost_with_customer_lifetime_", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"1ba6a8ae-0a48-5bfc-98b5-932836f5c3c3", kc_id:"1ba6a8ae-0a48-5bfc-98b5-932836f5c3c3", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"apply", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Classify complex, dissonance-reducing, habitual, and variety-seeking buying using both involvement and perceived brand differentiation. Source: section 3.1, printed page 94.", label:"Use involvement and perceived brand differences", canonical_key:"use_involvement_and_perceived_brand_differences", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"91bafb5c-a55d-5096-8def-3dc2db027033", kc_id:"91bafb5c-a55d-5096-8def-3dc2db027033", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"relationship", definition:"Distinguish physiological, safety, social, esteem, and self-actualization motives in a purchase without assuming identical motivation for all consumers. Source: section 3.2, printed page 97.", label:"Analyze Maslow's five need categories", canonical_key:"analyze_maslow_s_five_need_categories", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"8d9cf145-ef8a-543f-9bc9-165da9337a97", kc_id:"8d9cf145-ef8a-543f-9bc9-165da9337a97", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"relationship", definition:"Identify the gap between a consumer's actual and desired state and distinguish internal from external triggers. Source: section 3.3, printed page 111.", label:"Diagnose need recognition", canonical_key:"diagnose_need_recognition", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"9b417b62-88f3-5534-be4b-8b2747012740", kc_id:"9b417b62-88f3-5534-be4b-8b2747012740", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"relationship", definition:"Compare memory-based internal search with information from personal, commercial, public, and experiential external sources. Source: section 3.3, printed page 111.", label:"Analyze consumer information search", canonical_key:"analyze_consumer_information_search", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"d2e02e08-f412-5631-9ee5-38e2e2f53b97", kc_id:"d2e02e08-f412-5631-9ee5-38e2e2f53b97", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Use relevant attributes and consumer priorities to compare a consideration set of offerings. Source: section 3.3, printed page 111.", label:"Evaluate alternatives and determinant criteria", canonical_key:"evaluate_alternatives_and_determinant_criteria", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"0efc737e-e640-59a3-a030-75e1b6dac2cc", kc_id:"0efc737e-e640-59a3-a030-75e1b6dac2cc", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"understand", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"relationship", definition:"Distinguish purchase intention from actual choice, allowing for intervening social and situational influences. Source: section 3.3, printed page 111.", label:"Explain the purchase decision", canonical_key:"explain_the_purchase_decision", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"a7b393e1-da7e-5d6b-88ef-7d3792e049d2", kc_id:"a7b393e1-da7e-5d6b-88ef-7d3792e049d2", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.59Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"relationship", definition:"Relate expectations, experienced performance, satisfaction, dissonance, and future behavior. Source: section 3.3, printed page 111.", label:"Analyze post-purchase evaluation", canonical_key:"analyze_post_purchase_evaluation", status:"approved"}}] AS row
