UNWIND [{concept_id:"3ef22325-1cc6-54b1-844c-16cd816ed76f", kc_id:"3ef22325-1cc6-54b1-844c-16cd816ed76f", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 4, Closing Company Case, task 3. Case context: Corporate Medical Services Corporate Medical Services (CMS) was established in Tennessee on October 1, 1995, with one person, one computer, and one client.28 The company was started with the goal of providing Department of Transportation (DOT) customers with a resource to meet new drug testing requirements. “The…. Learner task: More Security, Less Hassle “Dealing with governmental regulations and requirements is no easy task. We have developed processes, procedures, and performance benchmarks to deal with the complexity of this industry so that you don’t have to. At the end of the day, you will be confident that your program is operating the way it should.”", label:"Ch. 4 Closing Company Case, task 3: More Security, Less Hassle “Dealing with governmental regulations and requirements is…", canonical_key:"ch_4_closing_company_case_task_3_more_security_l", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"8771fca6-a10c-5350-a80e-82fdc7c4eb9a", kc_id:"8771fca6-a10c-5350-a80e-82fdc7c4eb9a", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 4, Closing Company Case, task 4. Case context: Corporate Medical Services Corporate Medical Services (CMS) was established in Tennessee on October 1, 1995, with one person, one computer, and one client.28 The company was started with the goal of providing Department of Transportation (DOT) customers with a resource to meet new drug testing requirements. “The…. Learner task: Respect “We are here to serve our clients. To successfully accomplish that goal, we treat our staff, our clients, our vendors, and your donors with respect. In an industry where conversations can sometimes get tense, we handle every situation in a respectful and professional manner in order to mitigate any issues that may arise.”", label:"Ch. 4 Closing Company Case, task 4: Respect “We are here to serve our clients", canonical_key:"ch_4_closing_company_case_task_4_respect_we_are_", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"2759db32-dae0-5555-8208-7c83e932c4cb", kc_id:"2759db32-dae0-5555-8208-7c83e932c4cb", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 4, Closing Company Case, task 5. Case context: Corporate Medical Services Corporate Medical Services (CMS) was established in Tennessee on October 1, 1995, with one person, one computer, and one client.28 The company was started with the goal of providing Department of Transportation (DOT) customers with a resource to meet new drug testing requirements. “The…. Learner task: Speed of Technology “Our systems and processes are designed to get you the results you need as quickly as possible, which is why no one is faster at reporting drug screens. Our system averages a 7-minute turnaround on negative reports, once released from the lab.” As CMS looked for growth, it began to work with industry trade associations. The trucking industry was growing rapidly. Industry leaders were continuing to expand their fleets, and new trucking companies were entering the market. Providing drug and alcohol testing was not something the companies wanted to think about—until it was a necessity. Corporate safety managers could be difficult to reach; however, with a narrow focus and significant industry knowledge, CMS was well positioned to…", label:"Ch. 4 Closing Company Case, task 5: Speed of Technology “Our systems and processes are designed to get you the results you…", canonical_key:"ch_4_closing_company_case_task_5_speed_of_techno", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"24c41fd4-3538-5f47-bd04-8004344e4218", kc_id:"24c41fd4-3538-5f47-bd04-8004344e4218", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 4, Closing Company Case, task 1. Case context: Corporate Medical Services Corporate Medical Services (CMS) was established in Tennessee on October 1, 1995, with one person, one computer, and one client.28 The company was started with the goal of providing Department of Transportation (DOT) customers with a resource to meet new drug testing requirements. “The…. Learner task: Which characteristics of the B2B market are most evident for CMS?", label:"Ch. 4 Closing Company Case, task 1: Which characteristics of the B2B market are most evident for CMS", canonical_key:"ch_4_closing_company_case_task_1_which_character", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"6694a8a5-c31e-5085-9fa9-de21c374a6ca", kc_id:"6694a8a5-c31e-5085-9fa9-de21c374a6ca", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 4, Closing Company Case, task 2. Case context: Corporate Medical Services Corporate Medical Services (CMS) was established in Tennessee on October 1, 1995, with one person, one computer, and one client.28 The company was started with the goal of providing Department of Transportation (DOT) customers with a resource to meet new drug testing requirements. “The…. Learner task: If a trucking company wanted to buy services from CMS, what type of buying behavior would this be?", label:"Ch. 4 Closing Company Case, task 2: If a trucking company wanted to buy services from CMS, what type of buying behavior…", canonical_key:"ch_4_closing_company_case_task_2_if_a_trucking_c", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"a901ca8c-9edf-50c1-acfb-e064d71a90d2", kc_id:"a901ca8c-9edf-50c1-acfb-e064d71a90d2", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 4, Closing Company Case, task 3. Case context: Corporate Medical Services Corporate Medical Services (CMS) was established in Tennessee on October 1, 1995, with one person, one computer, and one client.28 The company was started with the goal of providing Department of Transportation (DOT) customers with a resource to meet new drug testing requirements. “The…. Learner task: List and describe the major B2B buying influences prevalent for the CMS market segment.", label:"Ch. 4 Closing Company Case, task 3: List and describe the major B2B buying influences prevalent for the CMS market segment.", canonical_key:"ch_4_closing_company_case_task_3_list_and_descri", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"87c68370-920a-56a3-bf1c-4ad54e34ea5b", kc_id:"87c68370-920a-56a3-bf1c-4ad54e34ea5b", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 4, Closing Company Case, task 4. Case context: Corporate Medical Services Corporate Medical Services (CMS) was established in Tennessee on October 1, 1995, with one person, one computer, and one client.28 The company was started with the goal of providing Department of Transportation (DOT) customers with a resource to meet new drug testing requirements. “The…. Learner task: List three ways Corporate Medical Services can become a leading contender in the supplier search stage of the B2B buying process.", label:"Ch. 4 Closing Company Case, task 4: List three ways Corporate Medical Services can become a leading contender in the…", canonical_key:"ch_4_closing_company_case_task_4_list_three_ways", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"38fb4f28-a25e-5aaf-9627-59fcc83c3068", kc_id:"38fb4f28-a25e-5aaf-9627-59fcc83c3068", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 5, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 1. Learner task: Somewhat like the cola wars of the 1980s, quick-service food chains are engaging in chicken wars. List and discuss at least two ways Chick-fil-A, Popeye’s, and Slim Chickens have differentiated and positioned their products as they fight for customers.", label:"Ch. 5 Discussion Questions, task 1: Somewhat like the cola wars of the 1980s, quick-service food chains are engaging in…", canonical_key:"ch_5_discussion_questions_task_1_somewhat_like_t", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"356245bb-71dd-5056-8d0d-c0f7de3d0ced", kc_id:"356245bb-71dd-5056-8d0d-c0f7de3d0ced", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 5, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 2. Learner task: Why would a local hair salon choose to use geographic segmentation variables and a narrow, concentrated marketing strategy rather than psychographic, demographic, or behavioral variables plus undifferentiated, differentiated, or micromarketing strategies? Might the salon be more successful at reaching its target audience by utilizing multi-segment marketing?", label:"Ch. 5 Discussion Questions, task 2: Why would a local hair salon choose to use geographic segmentation variables and a…", canonical_key:"ch_5_discussion_questions_task_2_why_would_a_loc", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"b9bcd263-754f-5a15-9837-6014c92a2131", kc_id:"b9bcd263-754f-5a15-9837-6014c92a2131", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 5, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 3. Learner task: Describe the major elements of a positioning statement. Which words in the following Walt Disney World positioning statement—“For the young and young-at-heart, Walt Disney World is the theme park that best delivers on an immersive and magical experience because Walt Disney World, and only Walt Disney World, connects you to the characters and worlds you most desire”—illustrate what Disney World promises customers and why it delivers on this promise better than competitors in the entertainment industry?", label:"Ch. 5 Discussion Questions, task 3: Describe the major elements of a positioning statement", canonical_key:"ch_5_discussion_questions_task_3_describe_the_ma", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"af5d28ae-b83f-53c8-8310-9385dd4556de", kc_id:"af5d28ae-b83f-53c8-8310-9385dd4556de", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 5, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 4. Learner task: Have you ever watched cartoons? If so, have you seen content that you would consider to be unethical targeting by advertisers? Common examples of ethical lapses include ethnic and racial profiling, promoting gender stereotypes, depicting violence, and encouraging child obesity.", label:"Ch. 5 Discussion Questions, task 4: Have you ever watched cartoons", canonical_key:"ch_5_discussion_questions_task_4_have_you_ever_w", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"f7769487-cb13-5a62-a640-dce584d9b1df", kc_id:"f7769487-cb13-5a62-a640-dce584d9b1df", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 5, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 1. Learner task: Mountain Dew was introduced in 1940 and marketed as “moonshine,” complete with Willy the Hillbilly proclaiming “It’ll tickle yore innards!” Since PepsiCo acquired the brand in the 1960s, Mountain Dew has cycled through new looks, logos, slogans, packaging, flavors, and brand personalities now connected with speed and velocity rather than soda brewed in a whiskey still. Research Mountain Dew’s history and consider this question: How has Mountain Dew steadily moved away from other competitors in the soft drink industry in its positioning efforts, and do you believe this movement has grown consumers’ brand loyalty?", label:"Ch. 5 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 1: Mountain Dew was introduced in 1940 and marketed as “moonshine,” complete with Willy…", canonical_key:"ch_5_critical_thinking_exercises_task_1_mountain", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"764154ba-adb5-5c83-a3b3-941d1b7fbd84", kc_id:"764154ba-adb5-5c83-a3b3-941d1b7fbd84", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"create", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 5, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 2. Learner task: The three-step STP model has proven successful in stepping systematically through the target market selection process. How has your college proceeded from segmentation to targeting to effectively positioning? Offer examples of each step and develop a perceptual map showing how the average high school student may perceive your college’s attributes versus its competitors’.", label:"Ch. 5 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 2: The three-step STP model has proven successful in stepping systematically through the…", canonical_key:"ch_5_critical_thinking_exercises_task_2_the_thre", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"bf6c31a6-746f-5b33-b872-eba7c8c0a4cd", kc_id:"bf6c31a6-746f-5b33-b872-eba7c8c0a4cd", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 5, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 3. Learner task: Why might candy companies such as Lemonhead, Ghirardelli, Jelly Belly, PEEPS, Mike and Ike, and Welch’s Fruit Snacks make the pledge not to advertise to children under the age of 12? Does this decision also send a message to parents?", label:"Ch. 5 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 3: Why might candy companies such as Lemonhead, Ghirardelli, Jelly Belly, PEEPS, Mike and…", canonical_key:"ch_5_critical_thinking_exercises_task_3_why_migh", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"83e7f943-094d-5ef0-bb33-50942eae61a4", kc_id:"83e7f943-094d-5ef0-bb33-50942eae61a4", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"create", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 5, Building Your Personal Brand, task 1. Learner task: There are numerous examples of successful personal brands. For good examples, read this article from the Webflow blog where 18 of the best personal brand examples in 2022 are listed. (https://openstax.org/r/ personalbrandingexamples) Using what you learned in this chapter about marketing to target markets and using the inspiration and knowledge gained from this article, write the opening page to your website. Keep in mind the things shared in the article on what made the personal brands stand out. And know your target market so you can craft a message that will appeal to them.", label:"Ch. 5 Building Your Personal Brand, task 1: There are numerous examples of successful personal brands", canonical_key:"ch_5_building_your_personal_brand_task_1_there_a", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"2f3927b7-8b5a-5556-8de5-c89e633fbbbd", kc_id:"2f3927b7-8b5a-5556-8de5-c89e633fbbbd", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 5, What Do Marketers Do?, task 1. Learner task: Utilize LinkedIn to find two sales managers in your geographic area and invite them to connect with you. Try using what you now know about segmentation, targeting, and positioning to consider industries you’d like to work in, where they might be located, and how you can make your resume appealing to them. Can you craft a compelling message that encourages sales managers to connect with you? Once linked, “interview” at least one sales professional and ask questions about what they enjoy most and least about their sales careers.", label:"Ch. 5 What Do Marketers Do?, task 1: Utilize LinkedIn to find two sales managers in your geographic area and invite them to…", canonical_key:"ch_5_what_do_marketers_do_task_1_utilize_linkedi", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"6c1e17c6-e87e-5743-bbda-880f76428134", kc_id:"6c1e17c6-e87e-5743-bbda-880f76428134", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"create", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 5, Marketing Plan Exercise, task 1. Learner task: Complete the following information about the company and products/services you chose to focus on as you develop the marketing plan throughout the course. You may need to conduct research in order to obtain necessary information. Instructions: Using the Marketing Plan Template file you created from the Marketing and Customer Value assignment and expanded upon in Strategic Planning in Marketing, complete the following sections of your marketing plan: • Market Segmentation • Target Market • Buyer Personas • Positioning Submit the marketing plan to your instructor for grading and feedback.", label:"Ch. 5 Marketing Plan Exercise, task 1: Complete the following information about the company and products/services you chose…", canonical_key:"ch_5_marketing_plan_exercise_task_1_complete_the", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"d98ebd9f-c007-555c-a70e-689564e83df1", kc_id:"d98ebd9f-c007-555c-a70e-689564e83df1", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 5, Closing Company Case, task 1. Case context: Travelers Point Distillery In early 2000, several friends got together to tell stories and drink bourbon. It was obvious that friends and stories come together with good bourbon. The best stories included the rich family history of Master Distiller Mel Lytton. Dating back to the 1880s and into prohibition, Mel’s…. Learner task: Based on the price point and branding for Travelers Point bourbon, what is the recommended method the company should use to segment its market?", label:"Ch. 5 Closing Company Case, task 1: Based on the price point and branding for Travelers Point bourbon, what is the…", canonical_key:"ch_5_closing_company_case_task_1_based_on_the_pr", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"c69bce7d-d391-59ca-8943-4941b2b928d5", kc_id:"c69bce7d-d391-59ca-8943-4941b2b928d5", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 5, Closing Company Case, task 2. Case context: Travelers Point Distillery In early 2000, several friends got together to tell stories and drink bourbon. It was obvious that friends and stories come together with good bourbon. The best stories included the rich family history of Master Distiller Mel Lytton. Dating back to the 1880s and into prohibition, Mel’s…. Learner task: Which target market strategy would you recommend for Travelers Point, and why?", label:"Ch. 5 Closing Company Case, task 2: Which target market strategy would you recommend for Travelers Point, and why", canonical_key:"ch_5_closing_company_case_task_2_which_target_ma", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"7d458ed2-d603-5313-aa80-1a766ee9b544", kc_id:"7d458ed2-d603-5313-aa80-1a766ee9b544", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 5, Closing Company Case, task 3. Case context: Travelers Point Distillery In early 2000, several friends got together to tell stories and drink bourbon. It was obvious that friends and stories come together with good bourbon. The best stories included the rich family history of Master Distiller Mel Lytton. Dating back to the 1880s and into prohibition, Mel’s…. Learner task: What approach to brand positioning do you recommend for Travelers Point? Support your answer.", label:"Ch. 5 Closing Company Case, task 3: What approach to brand positioning do you recommend for Travelers Point", canonical_key:"ch_5_closing_company_case_task_3_what_approach_t", status:"approved"}}] AS row
