UNWIND [{concept_id:"30e711c4-7cf2-5930-9620-e3336da2a0e1", kc_id:"30e711c4-7cf2-5930-9620-e3336da2a0e1", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 7, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 1. Learner task: Marketers must consider the global marketing environment when determining strategy. In addition to the international trade system, economic environment, and cultural norms, what other environmental factor is a critical consideration? Use an example to illustrate the importance of this environmental factor.", label:"Ch. 7 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 1: Marketers must consider the global marketing environment when determining strategy", canonical_key:"ch_7_critical_thinking_exercises_task_1_marketer", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"bc36f09d-cfb8-5100-a22f-6be347af4790", kc_id:"bc36f09d-cfb8-5100-a22f-6be347af4790", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 7, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 2. Learner task: Thousands of businesses must strike a balance between standardizing marketing practices on a global scale versus adapting products to local markets. List two companies within the same industry, such as Toyota and Volkswagen, that approach their global marketing strategy using product standardization or adaptation. Then check global sales to help determine which approach is most effective.", label:"Ch. 7 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 2: Thousands of businesses must strike a balance between standardizing marketing…", canonical_key:"ch_7_critical_thinking_exercises_task_2_thousand", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"7c88495a-e32b-5a03-89ee-f64d7ed555ee", kc_id:"7c88495a-e32b-5a03-89ee-f64d7ed555ee", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 7, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 3. Learner task: Procter & Gamble makes dozens of laundry detergents and adapts these products to market preferences around the world. Two of these brands include Ariel and Mif. Why might European markets prefer Ariel’s formulation and Russian markets demand Mif? Build a list of three reasons why Western Europe and Eastern Europe may differ in their laundry detergent preferences.", label:"Ch. 7 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 3: Procter & Gamble makes dozens of laundry detergents and adapts these products to…", canonical_key:"ch_7_critical_thinking_exercises_task_3_procter_", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"9dfe008c-66e7-5c8c-a814-ab4728f112de", kc_id:"9dfe008c-66e7-5c8c-a814-ab4728f112de", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 7, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 4. Learner task: You are working on a marketing campaign for the Japanese division of Malley’s Chocolates. You have created a pitch to top executives for a commercial featuring a Japanese husband surprising his wife in her bedroom on Valentine’s Day with a small box of chocolates containing four candies. Would this be a good idea for a commercial? Why or why not?", label:"Ch. 7 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 4: You are working on a marketing campaign for the Japanese division of Malley’s Chocolates", canonical_key:"ch_7_critical_thinking_exercises_task_4_you_are_", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"da565e5a-c226-5b92-93d9-7fac5ce4de00", kc_id:"da565e5a-c226-5b92-93d9-7fac5ce4de00", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"create", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 7, Building Your Personal Brand, task 1. Learner task: There are ways to build skills that will help you in international markets. Consider the items shared in this chapter and consider what you might do to enhance your skills. Then write a one-to-two-page document outlining a plan for what you will do to improve your skills. Be specific and include a timeline. You might also want to meet with international business instructors to help identify areas to include. Here are several things to consider: • Does your campus offer courses or workshops in diversity? Many diversity training opportunities also offer a certificate of completion that you can include in your resume. • Is there a foreign language requirement at your university? If so, this education plus a study abroad experience will reinforce your…", label:"Ch. 7 Building Your Personal Brand, task 1: There are ways to build skills that will help you in international markets", canonical_key:"ch_7_building_your_personal_brand_task_1_there_a", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"35201f01-7757-5cfe-b976-45a54c472ef7", kc_id:"35201f01-7757-5cfe-b976-45a54c472ef7", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"create", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 7, What Do Marketers Do?, task 1. Learner task: Part of the International Trade Administration, Export Assistance Centers (found in the United States, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and Asia) help US-based businesses plan, develop, and execute international strategies to succeed in today’s global marketplace through the. Find the center nearest to you (https://openstax.org/r/ uscommercialservice) and conduct a short interview with an export counselor there to learn more about their job. To learn more about global market opportunities through the International Trade Administration, watch the short video “Discover Global Markets.” Click to view content (https://openstax.org/books/principles-marketing/pages/7-what-do-marketers-do) Here are some questions to ask: • What services does the center…", label:"Ch. 7 What Do Marketers Do?, task 1: Part of the International Trade Administration, Export Assistance Centers (found in…", canonical_key:"ch_7_what_do_marketers_do_task_1_part_of_the_int", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"ca47e068-9b7f-534f-8e7f-af3403869438", kc_id:"ca47e068-9b7f-534f-8e7f-af3403869438", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 7, Closing Company Case, task 1. Case context: Timmy Global Health Founded in 1997 by Dr. Charles (Chuck) Dietzen, Timmy Global Health has a mission to empower communities to address health disparities in a sustainable way. For over two decades, Timmy has supported care sites across four countries in Latin America and Africa: Guatemala, Ecuador, the Dominican…. Learner task: To provide for the needs of underserved people in communities around the globe, Timmy Global Health faced many challenges. What are some of the most pressing challenges in the global landscape?", label:"Ch. 7 Closing Company Case, task 1: To provide for the needs of underserved people in communities around the globe, Timmy…", canonical_key:"ch_7_closing_company_case_task_1_to_provide_for_", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"731acf3f-d1a7-5d20-b098-e91f93c82018", kc_id:"731acf3f-d1a7-5d20-b098-e91f93c82018", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 7, Closing Company Case, task 2. Case context: Timmy Global Health Founded in 1997 by Dr. Charles (Chuck) Dietzen, Timmy Global Health has a mission to empower communities to address health disparities in a sustainable way. For over two decades, Timmy has supported care sites across four countries in Latin America and Africa: Guatemala, Ecuador, the Dominican…. Learner task: What are some of the global issues that have impacted Timmy Global Health and the work it does?", label:"Ch. 7 Closing Company Case, task 2: What are some of the global issues that have impacted Timmy Global Health and the work…", canonical_key:"ch_7_closing_company_case_task_2_what_are_some_o", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"1a8052e2-8e3d-568e-bc8d-ac18c346047c", kc_id:"1a8052e2-8e3d-568e-bc8d-ac18c346047c", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 7, Closing Company Case, task 3. Case context: Timmy Global Health Founded in 1997 by Dr. Charles (Chuck) Dietzen, Timmy Global Health has a mission to empower communities to address health disparities in a sustainable way. For over two decades, Timmy has supported care sites across four countries in Latin America and Africa: Guatemala, Ecuador, the Dominican…. Learner task: Marketers often have to adapt to international markets. What are some of the adaptations most prevalent for the work Timmy Global Health is doing?", label:"Ch. 7 Closing Company Case, task 3: Marketers often have to adapt to international markets", canonical_key:"ch_7_closing_company_case_task_3_marketers_often", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"014d6c10-cc06-5eb6-9bb7-a32c78e81f85", kc_id:"014d6c10-cc06-5eb6-9bb7-a32c78e81f85", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 7, Closing Company Case, task 4. Case context: Timmy Global Health Founded in 1997 by Dr. Charles (Chuck) Dietzen, Timmy Global Health has a mission to empower communities to address health disparities in a sustainable way. For over two decades, Timmy has supported care sites across four countries in Latin America and Africa: Guatemala, Ecuador, the Dominican…. Learner task: Ethical issues are always a concern for any company. When working internationally, ethics can be a challenge since practices in a home country may be very different than in a foreign country. What are some ethical issues that may pose difficulties for Timmy Global Health?", label:"Ch. 7 Closing Company Case, task 4: Ethical issues are always a concern for any company", canonical_key:"ch_7_closing_company_case_task_4_ethical_issues_", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"d8e2805c-045e-59af-894c-317809daab85", kc_id:"d8e2805c-045e-59af-894c-317809daab85", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 8, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 1. Learner task: The Special Olympics offers businesses the opportunity to sponsor local, regional, national, and international events. Using what you have learned from this chapter, list three reasons why companies such as Procter & Gamble, Toyota, Coca-Cola, United Airlines, Microsoft, and the NFL would choose to spend millions of marketing dollars to partner with Special Olympics.", label:"Ch. 8 Discussion Questions, task 1: The Special Olympics offers businesses the opportunity to sponsor local, regional,…", canonical_key:"ch_8_discussion_questions_task_1_the_special_oly", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"47967466-5cbd-568a-852d-8b7a260cde6f", kc_id:"47967466-5cbd-568a-852d-8b7a260cde6f", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 8, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 2. Learner task: The United States is moving swiftly to a “plurality nation” status, according to the US Census Bureau. Identify two major multicultural trends that have and will continue to impact market segmentation.", label:"Ch. 8 Discussion Questions, task 2: The United States is moving swiftly to a “plurality nation” status, according to the…", canonical_key:"ch_8_discussion_questions_task_2_the_united_stat", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"4576a3ed-40be-5496-b44a-158c46833f4c", kc_id:"4576a3ed-40be-5496-b44a-158c46833f4c", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 8, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 3. Learner task: Student Services on your campus likely has a diversity and inclusion staff that encourages an expansive range of cultural perspectives, experiences, voices, and methods for taking action on campus. How does your college or university market diversity and inclusion services to prospective students through its website?", label:"Ch. 8 Discussion Questions, task 3: Student Services on your campus likely has a diversity and inclusion staff that…", canonical_key:"ch_8_discussion_questions_task_3_student_service", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"c896ba72-73ef-56f0-bc18-be81527a56bc", kc_id:"c896ba72-73ef-56f0-bc18-be81527a56bc", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 8, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 4. Learner task: Market fragmentation is the concept that all markets are increasingly diverse and comprised of smaller segments of consumers that respond differently to marketing messages. Media, too, has splintered, and in addition to having access to information provided by newspapers, magazines, TV, and radio, consumers now have access to millions of informational sources. However, severe fragmentation of both consumers and ways to communicate with them poses many challenges in marketing efficiency and branding. Why?", label:"Ch. 8 Discussion Questions, task 4: Market fragmentation is the concept that all markets are increasingly diverse and…", canonical_key:"ch_8_discussion_questions_task_4_market_fragment", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"81392d06-1fe6-5ea4-b404-192f865b66a7", kc_id:"81392d06-1fe6-5ea4-b404-192f865b66a7", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 8, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 5. Learner task: DMiQ reveals that baby boomers offer the best marketing opportunities for firms. Which sociodemographic group offers the next best marketing opportunity by sheer size of the segment?", label:"Ch. 8 Discussion Questions, task 5: DMiQ reveals that baby boomers offer the best marketing opportunities for firms", canonical_key:"ch_8_discussion_questions_task_5_dmiq_reveals_th", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"0b1ffd1b-9f81-5e37-a0e4-fb26771c155a", kc_id:"0b1ffd1b-9f81-5e37-a0e4-fb26771c155a", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"create", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 8, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 1. Learner task: Like Nike’s marketing adaptation with “Nike by You,” other retailers offer customers individualized products. For instance, you can design your own jeans (https://openstax.org/r/makeyourownjeans) online. Brainstorm five other products that may lend themselves to customized offerings that express cultural or sociodemographic differences.", label:"Ch. 8 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 1: Like Nike’s marketing adaptation with “Nike by You,” other retailers offer customers…", canonical_key:"ch_8_critical_thinking_exercises_task_1_like_nik", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"5c6f7797-35ff-518a-9ee1-c070c546cacc", kc_id:"5c6f7797-35ff-518a-9ee1-c070c546cacc", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 8, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 2. Learner task: Diversity marketing intelligence (DMiQ) refers to the capability of identifying, accepting, and valuing the diversity of consumers within a market and using this knowledge to tailor the marketing mix accordingly. Thus, capturing insights about consumers’ heritage, experience, lifestyle, beliefs, or living situations helps explain the nuances and idiosyncrasies associated with diversity. These insights helped identify that the LGBTQIA+ community generally spends more money online and at retail stores. Additionally, the research firm Out Now estimates the LGBTQIA+ community spends more than $211 billion on travel. How can the travel industry employ DMiQ to derive more value from this group that enjoys travel and is willing to pay for it?", label:"Ch. 8 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 2: Diversity marketing intelligence (DMiQ) refers to the capability of identifying,…", canonical_key:"ch_8_critical_thinking_exercises_task_2_diversit", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"db425d5b-57df-5a76-b0d5-6bba7fb42bbf", kc_id:"db425d5b-57df-5a76-b0d5-6bba7fb42bbf", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 8, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 3. Learner task: Research has shown that members of the baby boomer generation possess the most wealth in the United States and are responsible for 70 percent of annual spending on prescriptions and medical supplies. Are there any ethical considerations in developing marketing messages to this large and older segment of society that doesn’t want to be pigeonholed as “elderly”?", label:"Ch. 8 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 3: Research has shown that members of the baby boomer generation possess the most wealth…", canonical_key:"ch_8_critical_thinking_exercises_task_3_research", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"ae4c3d73-3861-5062-bddf-8171f2b16a30", kc_id:"ae4c3d73-3861-5062-bddf-8171f2b16a30", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"create", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 8, Building Your Personal Brand, task 1. Learner task: Students who are building their résumés have always been encouraged to set themselves apart from the competition for internships, jobs, and volunteer experiences. In other words, focus on what makes you stand out from other job seekers. If you are bilingual, why not prepare your résumé, blog, or LinkedIn profile in both languages? Are you especially knowledgeable in a particular area such as designing alternate reality games? Do you collect comic books or baseball trading cards? All of these interests, collections, and abilities not only have the potential to create a dialogue with potential employers, but they also highlight your heritage, lifestyle, or singularity to your advantage.", label:"Ch. 8 Building Your Personal Brand, task 1: Students who are building their résumés have always been encouraged to set themselves…", canonical_key:"ch_8_building_your_personal_brand_task_1_student", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"393b6996-9c5b-5767-be9a-e99d5b44e639", kc_id:"393b6996-9c5b-5767-be9a-e99d5b44e639", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 8, What Do Marketers Do?, task 1. Learner task: Relatively few recent marketing graduates think about entering the nonprofit arena. Some of the key positions in nonprofits include marketing director, event coordinator, director of development, communications specialist, and volunteer coordinator. There are many nonprofit organizations operating in the United States that strive to serve multicultural groups and sociodemographic communities. Some have purposeful objectives like equitable rights and inclusivity. Some national examples include Advancement Project, American Civil Liberties Union (ACLU), Asian Americans Advancing Justice (AAJC), Equal Justice Initiative (EJI), Human Rights Campaign Foundation, League of United Latin American Citizens (LULAC), National Association for the Advancement…", label:"Ch. 8 What Do Marketers Do?, task 1: Relatively few recent marketing graduates think about entering the nonprofit arena", canonical_key:"ch_8_what_do_marketers_do_task_1_relatively_few_", status:"approved"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Concept{concept_id: row.concept_id, kc_id: row.kc_id}) SET n += row.properties SET n:KnowledgeComponent;
UNWIND [{concept_id:"0f7cc007-87b1-51f4-9050-4054ff989195", kc_id:"0f7cc007-87b1-51f4-9050-4054ff989195", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 8, Closing Company Case, task 1. Case context: Lineout If 50 is the new 30, most 50-year-olds want to look 30. Consumers in their twenties want to look like their favorite Hollywood star or Instagram influencer. New methods, procedures, and products are flooding the market to appeal to the market demand for better skin, reduced facial wrinkles, and improved…. Learner task: How does Lineout adapt its marketing for each of the diverse markets it serves?", label:"Ch. 8 Closing Company Case, task 1: How does Lineout adapt its marketing for each of the diverse markets it serves", canonical_key:"ch_8_closing_company_case_task_1_how_does_lineou", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"c1ca93db-1197-50f9-901d-7956d298f29f", kc_id:"c1ca93db-1197-50f9-901d-7956d298f29f", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 8, Closing Company Case, task 2. Case context: Lineout If 50 is the new 30, most 50-year-olds want to look 30. Consumers in their twenties want to look like their favorite Hollywood star or Instagram influencer. New methods, procedures, and products are flooding the market to appeal to the market demand for better skin, reduced facial wrinkles, and improved…. Learner task: The trend in noninvasive cosmetic procedures grows every year. What are some of the factors that have impacted the demand for facial fillers?", label:"Ch. 8 Closing Company Case, task 2: The trend in noninvasive cosmetic procedures grows every year", canonical_key:"ch_8_closing_company_case_task_2_the_trend_in_no", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"a98f90d3-aebc-5ba2-92fc-021053bf8336", kc_id:"a98f90d3-aebc-5ba2-92fc-021053bf8336", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 8, Closing Company Case, task 3. Case context: Lineout If 50 is the new 30, most 50-year-olds want to look 30. Consumers in their twenties want to look like their favorite Hollywood star or Instagram influencer. New methods, procedures, and products are flooding the market to appeal to the market demand for better skin, reduced facial wrinkles, and improved…. Learner task: What are the factors Lineout is considering when looking at how it changes its marketing to meet the needs of its different consumer markets?", label:"Ch. 8 Closing Company Case, task 3: What are the factors Lineout is considering when looking at how it changes its…", canonical_key:"ch_8_closing_company_case_task_3_what_are_the_fa", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"44a0f4c5-020a-5fca-948d-e7a0ea16f611", kc_id:"44a0f4c5-020a-5fca-948d-e7a0ea16f611", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 8, Closing Company Case, task 4. Case context: Lineout If 50 is the new 30, most 50-year-olds want to look 30. Consumers in their twenties want to look like their favorite Hollywood star or Instagram influencer. New methods, procedures, and products are flooding the market to appeal to the market demand for better skin, reduced facial wrinkles, and improved…. Learner task: The various consumer groups Lineout is serving have different and unique concerns. What are some of the factors that have created the concerns?", label:"Ch. 8 Closing Company Case, task 4: The various consumer groups Lineout is serving have different and unique concerns", canonical_key:"ch_8_closing_company_case_task_4_the_various_con", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"f0a4ec95-b52f-52b2-a648-db26ff6bee62", kc_id:"f0a4ec95-b52f-52b2-a648-db26ff6bee62", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 9, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 1. Learner task: Think of a product that you have used recently. What are the core, actual, and augmented products?", label:"Ch. 9 Discussion Questions, task 1: Think of a product that you have used recently", canonical_key:"ch_9_discussion_questions_task_1_think_of_a_prod", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"cbb78a81-ddbe-586e-9d8c-3b4733b62c88", kc_id:"cbb78a81-ddbe-586e-9d8c-3b4733b62c88", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 9, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 2. Learner task: How would you promote a shopping product differently than a specialty product?", label:"Ch. 9 Discussion Questions, task 2: How would you promote a shopping product differently than a specialty product", canonical_key:"ch_9_discussion_questions_task_2_how_would_you_p", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"17adac1e-3a25-5227-ac76-8eabcce0359e", kc_id:"17adac1e-3a25-5227-ac76-8eabcce0359e", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 9, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 3. Learner task: Look at the Oreo product line. Why are there so many products? What purpose does this variety serve?", label:"Ch. 9 Discussion Questions, task 3: Look at the Oreo product line", canonical_key:"ch_9_discussion_questions_task_3_look_at_the_ore", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"4f1b2bdd-57f5-5f5a-a9d4-81dac89062a0", kc_id:"4f1b2bdd-57f5-5f5a-a9d4-81dac89062a0", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 9, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 4. Learner task: Consider the Sears brand. Which stage of the product life cycle is Sears currently in? What do you recommend it do to change this stage?", label:"Ch. 9 Discussion Questions, task 4: Consider the Sears brand", canonical_key:"ch_9_discussion_questions_task_4_consider_the_se", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"b133b183-11b8-5555-bbc2-909037435715", kc_id:"b133b183-11b8-5555-bbc2-909037435715", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 9, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 5. Learner task: Discuss a brand to which you are loyal. Why are you loyal to the brand? How does the brand contribute to your loyalty?", label:"Ch. 9 Discussion Questions, task 5: Discuss a brand to which you are loyal", canonical_key:"ch_9_discussion_questions_task_5_discuss_a_brand", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"515aa119-56e3-538d-96dc-fa706a80e892", kc_id:"515aa119-56e3-538d-96dc-fa706a80e892", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 9, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 6. Learner task: Would you consider yourself a switcher, shifting loyal, split loyal, or hard-core loyal for your favorite brand? Why?", label:"Ch. 9 Discussion Questions, task 6: Would you consider yourself a switcher, shifting loyal, split loyal, or hard-core…", canonical_key:"ch_9_discussion_questions_task_6_would_you_consi", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"f35b1e59-715b-5c5c-bba5-1fc4909b5915", kc_id:"f35b1e59-715b-5c5c-bba5-1fc4909b5915", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 9, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 7. Learner task: Look at the Apple brand packaging in this chapter. How does this packaging meet the criteria that we discuss in the chapter?", label:"Ch. 9 Discussion Questions, task 7: Look at the Apple brand packaging in this chapter", canonical_key:"ch_9_discussion_questions_task_7_look_at_the_app", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"72e995cb-e24d-5ebb-aac5-af1abb928e68", kc_id:"72e995cb-e24d-5ebb-aac5-af1abb928e68", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 9, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 8. Learner task: Review Boxed Water Is Better’s website (https://openstax.org/r/boxedwaterisbetter). How do the website and packaging address environmental concerns?", label:"Ch. 9 Discussion Questions, task 8: Review Boxed Water Is Better’s website (https://openstax.org/r/boxedwaterisbetter)", canonical_key:"ch_9_discussion_questions_task_8_review_boxed_wa", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"5f650a2e-e848-5f17-a8b5-0d16d5d5136d", kc_id:"5f650a2e-e848-5f17-a8b5-0d16d5d5136d", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 9, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 9. Learner task: Discuss a brand’s packaging. How could the brand reduce its packaging or introduce recyclable packaging?", label:"Ch. 9 Discussion Questions, task 9: Discuss a brand’s packaging", canonical_key:"ch_9_discussion_questions_task_9_discuss_a_brand", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"63c646d4-7c56-51d3-b9eb-617058ce90d8", kc_id:"63c646d4-7c56-51d3-b9eb-617058ce90d8", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 9, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 10. Learner task: Why are safety statements important on packaging? What might you add to product safety statements?", label:"Ch. 9 Discussion Questions, task 10: Why are safety statements important on packaging", canonical_key:"ch_9_discussion_questions_task_10_why_are_safety", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"657f681a-88cf-547d-a86d-0090a8136e0d", kc_id:"657f681a-88cf-547d-a86d-0090a8136e0d", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 9, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 1. Learner task: Brainstorm purchases that you have made this week. Classify each into convenience products, shopping products, specialty products, or unsought products.", label:"Ch. 9 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 1: Brainstorm purchases that you have made this week", canonical_key:"ch_9_critical_thinking_exercises_task_1_brainsto", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"02ea8e43-d955-5d8b-8eec-628df53047f4", kc_id:"02ea8e43-d955-5d8b-8eec-628df53047f4", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 9, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 2. Learner task: Explain the product life cycle. How and why might it change based on certain criteria?", label:"Ch. 9 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 2: Explain the product life cycle", canonical_key:"ch_9_critical_thinking_exercises_task_2_explain_", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"2c67f714-c9ff-5694-967d-ad77734ee02c", kc_id:"2c67f714-c9ff-5694-967d-ad77734ee02c", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 9, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 3. Learner task: Examine the package of a product that you have in your pantry at home. Determine how the packaging aligns with the brand, protects the product, and displays value.", label:"Ch. 9 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 3: Examine the package of a product that you have in your pantry at home", canonical_key:"ch_9_critical_thinking_exercises_task_3_examine_", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"5c92eb11-8cbf-5e7b-9533-f73a41d60fbb", kc_id:"5c92eb11-8cbf-5e7b-9533-f73a41d60fbb", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"create", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 9, Building Your Personal Brand, task 1. Learner task: Can you honestly say that you “own” who you are? Do your habits and mannerisms belong to you? Are you comfortable in your skin? In her TED Talk, Harvard professor Amy Cuddy discusses how body language impacts how others perceive you. Our nonverbals give others a perception about who we are and how we are feeling. Our body language conveys dominance, much like animals do to show their power. Our posture and the space that we take up signals confidence. But sometimes we take cues from others. If our conversation partner is showing dominance, our body language might shrink in response. It turns out that posing for dominance changes the way we think and act. So use body language to your advantage next time you are trying to make an impression.17 Watch…", label:"Ch. 9 Building Your Personal Brand, task 1: Can you honestly say that you “own” who you are", canonical_key:"ch_9_building_your_personal_brand_task_1_can_you", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"49d1e23c-55a3-55d3-9314-dd1621a11091", kc_id:"49d1e23c-55a3-55d3-9314-dd1621a11091", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 9, What Do Marketers Do?, task 1. Case context: A product manager is the keeper of a brand. Their job is to develop the product strategy—the what, where, when, and how much of a product. Then, a product manager coordinates a cross-functional team of professionals from marketing, development, finance, legal, operations, manufacturing, supply chain, and more to…. Learner task: What is their philosophy on successful product management from launch through the product life cycle?", label:"Ch. 9 What Do Marketers Do?, task 1: What is their philosophy on successful product management from launch through the…", canonical_key:"ch_9_what_do_marketers_do_task_1_what_is_their_p", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"053f184e-ad34-5b51-815c-0560f09992a0", kc_id:"053f184e-ad34-5b51-815c-0560f09992a0", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 9, What Do Marketers Do?, task 2. Case context: A product manager is the keeper of a brand. Their job is to develop the product strategy—the what, where, when, and how much of a product. Then, a product manager coordinates a cross-functional team of professionals from marketing, development, finance, legal, operations, manufacturing, supply chain, and more to…. Learner task: What does their job entail? Who are the key members of their product ecosystem?", label:"Ch. 9 What Do Marketers Do?, task 2: What does their job entail", canonical_key:"ch_9_what_do_marketers_do_task_2_what_does_their", status:"approved"}}] AS row
