, level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 9, Closing Company Case, task 4. Case context: Ramblewood In 2018, husband and wife duo Zach and Riley McDonald began getting a flood of requests to help with events. Each of them individually had significant talents. They were great foodies, and they understood good food both in taste and in presentation. Their combined skill for aesthetics in design, display,…. Learner task: Brands are built in the hearts and minds of the customers. Successful brands engage customers on a personal level, connecting to their emotions and needs. Name some of the strategies Ramblewood uses to create its brand.", label:"Ch. 9 Closing Company Case, task 4: Brands are built in the hearts and minds of the customers", canonical_key:"ch_9_closing_company_case_task_4_brands_are_buil", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"ef29ab12-4552-52de-9798-bab62eb576dc", kc_id:"ef29ab12-4552-52de-9798-bab62eb576dc", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 10, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 1. Learner task: Explain the differences in: a. Continuous innovation b. Dynamically continuous innovation c. Discontinuous innovation", label:"Ch. 10 Discussion Questions, task 1: Explain the differences in: a", canonical_key:"ch_10_discussion_questions_task_1_explain_the_di", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"92de318d-e1e3-5917-8e9c-e0729704ca61", kc_id:"92de318d-e1e3-5917-8e9c-e0729704ca61", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 10, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 2. Learner task: List the stages of new product development.", label:"Ch. 10 Discussion Questions, task 2: List the stages of new product development.", canonical_key:"ch_10_discussion_questions_task_2_list_the_stage", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"b224a6a5-d1f8-5ca4-8eec-7d2e66536108", kc_id:"b224a6a5-d1f8-5ca4-8eec-7d2e66536108", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 10, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 3. Learner task: Consider new product adopter categories and answer the following questions. a. Do you believe that consumers are always in the same category? For example, once a laggard, always a laggard? Can someone be a laggard in one category and an early majority in another? b. What impact do these categories have on new product development? c. Can you think of a time or product category where marketing would want to push more consumers into one category?", label:"Ch. 10 Discussion Questions, task 3: Consider new product adopter categories and answer the following questions", canonical_key:"ch_10_discussion_questions_task_3_consider_new_p", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"182d64d6-a9c3-5672-9b19-4a539dbee92f", kc_id:"182d64d6-a9c3-5672-9b19-4a539dbee92f", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 10, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 1. Learner task: From a consumer perspective, what motivates you to try a new product? What new products have you tried in the last year? Did you continue to purchase them after the initial trial?", label:"Ch. 10 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 1: From a consumer perspective, what motivates you to try a new product", canonical_key:"ch_10_critical_thinking_exercises_task_1_from_a_", status:"approved"