llege project and that you’d like to interview them. There are hundreds of product development professionals, and you will quickly find that professionals in this field love to…. Learner task: What product have you worked on that you are most proud of or excited about?", label:"Ch. 10 What Do Marketers Do?, task 5: What product have you worked on that you are most proud of or excited about", canonical_key:"ch_10_what_do_marketers_do_task_5_what_product_h", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"1da06e65-23f3-5052-8158-075165aed310", kc_id:"1da06e65-23f3-5052-8158-075165aed310", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 10, What Do Marketers Do?, task 6. Case context: Using an online networking platform—for example, LinkedIn—network and connect with someone in product development. Explain that you have a college project and that you’d like to interview them. There are hundreds of product development professionals, and you will quickly find that professionals in this field love to…. Learner task: What product did you work on that failed? What did you learn in that process?", label:"Ch. 10 What Do Marketers Do?, task 6: What product did you work on that failed", canonical_key:"ch_10_what_do_marketers_do_task_6_what_product_d", status:"approved"}}] AS row
