3f964c", kc_id:"ff9d4daa-b2a7-562a-99aa-e344e73f964c", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 11, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 2. Learner task: Take the information that you have learned about internal and external marketing and describe two instances where as a student you have noticed excellent and poor marketing strategies. Are they internal or external, and why did you feel the way you did about them?", label:"Ch. 11 Discussion Questions, task 2: Take the information that you have learned about internal and external marketing and…", canonical_key:"ch_11_discussion_questions_task_2_take_the_infor", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"cb38c057-7e4d-5f42-82a0-049689853b22", kc_id:"cb38c057-7e4d-5f42-82a0-049689853b22", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"create", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 11, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 3. Learner task: Consider service variability instances where you were a customer and noticed exceptional service and poor service. For each instance, answer the following questions: a. Were you surprised? b. What specifically made you notice? c. Had you had this experience before with this company or another company? d. What response did you have? For instance, did you compliment? Tip? Complain? Do nothing? And why? e. If you were the company owner, what kind of training program would you develop to address the poor service you experienced? What might you implement as a reward for exceptional service? Why?", label:"Ch. 11 Discussion Questions, task 3: Consider service variability instances where you were a customer and noticed…", canonical_key:"ch_11_discussion_questions_task_3_consider_servi", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"e0a4b14d-b71d-5e5e-96d5-101c6c5e0612", kc_id:"e0a4b14d-b71d-5e5e-96d5-101c6c5e0612", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 11, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 4. Learner task: Analyze the differences between internal and external marketing. a. Define both terms. b. Consider and list the positive impact that both internal and external marketing can have on an organization.", label:"Ch. 11 Discussion Questions, task 4: Analyze the differences between internal and external marketing", canonical_key:"ch_11_discussion_questions_task_4_analyze_the_di", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"c6eaece7-71b5-5b60-a40e-1444ef448589", kc_id:"c6eaece7-71b5-5b60-a40e-1444ef448589", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 11, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 1. Learner task: Agree or disagree with the following statement: I tip for service based solely on the amount of the bill, not on things like quality of service, timing, etc. Discuss or make a list of the reasons why you agree or disagree.", label:"Ch. 11 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 1: Agree or disagree with the following statement: I tip for service based solely on the…", canonical_key:"ch_11_critical_thinking_exercises_task_1_agree_o", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"9d24f8b8-8b91-5132-b35c-b7dc7c10c6dc", kc_id:"9d24f8b8-8b91-5132-b35c-b7dc7c10c6dc", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 11, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 2. Learner task: Nordstrom’s reputation was built upon its value proposition of superior service. The company has maintained a high level of service over the years. Research other retailers that have a similar service- oriented value proposition. It could be a car company, restaurant, clothing store, etc. In looking at the changing demographics, do you believe that this level of service will continue to be perceived as value? If not, what will take its place?", label:"Ch. 11 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 2: Nordstrom’s reputation was built upon its value proposition of superior service", canonical_key:"ch_11_critical_thinking_exercises_task_2_nordstr", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"768d0e5b-236e-5046-b3fa-0226abb84802", kc_id:"768d0e5b-236e-5046-b3fa-0226abb84802", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 11, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 3. Learner task: Have you ever experienced service that was so poor that you did not return? Compare your views with someone that you know. Is this a common service issue?", label:"Ch. 11 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 3: Have you ever experienced service that was so poor that you did not return", canonical_key:"ch_11_critical_thinking_exercises_task_3_have_yo", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"27757f23-9bd0-59d1-b794-4d635c70c342", kc_id:"27757f23-9bd0-59d1-b794-4d635c70c342", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"create", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 11, Building Your Personal Brand, task 1. Learner task: “Communication is the act or process of using words, sounds, signs, or behaviors to express or exchange information or to express your ideas, thoughts, feelings, etc., to someone else.”50 What type of communicator are you? Analytical? Intuitive? Functional? Personal? Research communication styles and describe which best describes you. Outline a plan on how you might communicate with those who adhere to a different style. To get started, try this free communication style assessment (https://openstax.org/r/communicationstyles). There are also other assessments available online, so try a few and see and see if there are any differences. Keep in mind that communication also includes nonverbal signs such as our facial expressions and body language. How…", label:"Ch. 11 Building Your Personal Brand, task 1: “Communication is the act or process of using words, sounds, signs, or behaviors to…", canonical_key:"ch_11_building_your_personal_brand_task_1_commun", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"c43f52c7-e2ba-5285-b329-f5752ee678f3", kc_id:"c43f52c7-e2ba-5285-b329-f5752ee678f3", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 11, What Do Marketers Do?, task 1. Case context: Considering that “70% of small businesses are operated and owned by a single person,” the question arises: Who is doing the marketing?51 Find at least two small service businesses, one that you know to be successful and one that might be hanging on by a thread (hair salons, dry cleaners, mechanics, party planners,…. Learner task: Do they consider what they do to promote their business as marketing?", label:"Ch. 11 What Do Marketers Do?, task 1: Do they consider what they do to promote their business as marketing", canonical_key:"ch_11_what_do_marketers_do_task_1_do_they_consid", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"4bd7fb3a-a118-5221-9f09-47bdc18076b3", kc_id:"4bd7fb3a-a118-5221-9f09-47bdc18076b3", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datet