nsidering that “70% of small businesses are operated and owned by a single person,” the question arises: Who is doing the marketing?51 Find at least two small service businesses, one that you know to be successful and one that might be hanging on by a thread (hair salons, dry cleaners, mechanics, party planners,…. Learner task: What are the main activities that they do to market their business?", label:"Ch. 11 What Do Marketers Do?, task 4: What are the main activities that they do to market their business", canonical_key:"ch_11_what_do_marketers_do_task_4_what_are_the_m", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"d617c801-89cc-5ba5-8258-820bff851f50", kc_id:"d617c801-89cc-5ba5-8258-820bff851f50", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 11, What Do Marketers Do?, task 5. Case context: Considering that “70% of small businesses are operated and owned by a single person,” the question arises: Who is doing the marketing?51 Find at least two small service businesses, one that you know to be successful and one that might be hanging on by a thread (hair salons, dry cleaners, mechanics, party planners,…. Learner task: Do they have a formal business plan? A budget?", label:"Ch. 11 What Do Marketers Do?, task 5: Do they have a formal business plan", canonical_key:"ch_11_what_do_marketers_do_task_5_do_they_have_a", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"3a0bf3d1-0b94-535c-87eb-a4744ebca98c", kc_id:"3a0bf3d1-0b94-535c-87eb-a4744ebca98c", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 11, What Do Marketers Do?, task 6. Case context: Considering that “70% of small businesses are operated and owned by a single person,” the question arises: Who is doing the marketing?51 Find at least two small service businesses, one that you know to be successful and one that might be hanging on by a thread (hair salons, dry cleaners, mechanics, party planners,…. Learner task: How do they figure out what their budget should look like?", label:"Ch. 11 What Do Marketers Do?, task 6: How do they figure out what their budget should look like", canonical_key:"ch_11_what_do_marketers_do_task_6_how_do_they_fi", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"fdbe391a-6e82-59d5-bc3a-8e78c2f53b79", kc_id:"fdbe391a-6e82-59d5-bc3a-8e78c2f53b79", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 11, What Do Marketers Do?, task 7. Case context: Considering that “70% of small businesses are operated and owned by a single person,” the question arises: Who is doing the marketing?51 Find at least two small service businesses, one that you know to be successful and one that might be hanging on by a thread (hair salons, dry cleaners, mechanics, party planners,…. Learner task: Are there efforts that they consider successful and anything that seriously did not work?", label:"Ch. 11 What Do Marketers Do?, task 7: Are there efforts that they consider successful and anything that seriously did not work", canonical_key:"ch_11_what_do_marketers_do_task_7_are_there_effo", status:"approved"}}] AS row
