UNWIND [{concept_id:"941562a9-8990-5e29-9a8d-9059fceecd0c", kc_id:"941562a9-8990-5e29-9a8d-9059fceecd0c", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 11, What Do Marketers Do?, task 8. Case context: Considering that “70% of small businesses are operated and owned by a single person,” the question arises: Who is doing the marketing?51 Find at least two small service businesses, one that you know to be successful and one that might be hanging on by a thread (hair salons, dry cleaners, mechanics, party planners,…. Learner task: Do they respond to the marketing of their competitors? Of course, there are additional questions that you can ask as time permits. The idea here is to get a good look at what the challenges are to marketing a small business. Is this something that you see yourself doing—perhaps even as a business of your own?", label:"Ch. 11 What Do Marketers Do?, task 8: Do they respond to the marketing of their competitors", canonical_key:"ch_11_what_do_marketers_do_task_8_do_they_respon", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"41646d23-9e44-560d-b45d-1f1ca6aa7999", kc_id:"41646d23-9e44-560d-b45d-1f1ca6aa7999", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 11, Closing Company Case, task 1. Case context: Adventist Health Castle Adventist Health Castle in Kailua, Hawaii, is an award-winning hospital focused on serving the mind, body, and spirit of its patients. The 300 physicians provide services to the entire island of Oahu, following the mission to “care for the community and share God’s love.”52 Adventist Health…. Learner task: Adventist Health Castle is a health system operating to serve the population of Oahu. How would you classify its services?", label:"Ch. 11 Closing Company Case, task 1: Adventist Health Castle is a health system operating to serve the population of Oahu", canonical_key:"ch_11_closing_company_case_task_1_adventist_heal", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"f2f7775d-b763-5c61-baa0-61a864fa5f97", kc_id:"f2f7775d-b763-5c61-baa0-61a864fa5f97", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 11, Closing Company Case, task 2. Case context: Adventist Health Castle Adventist Health Castle in Kailua, Hawaii, is an award-winning hospital focused on serving the mind, body, and spirit of its patients. The 300 physicians provide services to the entire island of Oahu, following the mission to “care for the community and share God’s love.”52 Adventist Health…. Learner task: When community members choose to take a class on diabetes management, they are learning about diabetes from a clinical nurse instructor. The instructor informs the participants of the health risks associated with unhealthy lifestyle choices. Different clinical nurse instructors teach the classes each time. Depending on who teaches the course, the participants may learn the risks of a sedentary lifestyle. This is an example of which service characteristic?", label:"Ch. 11 Closing Company Case, task 2: When community members choose to take a class on diabetes management, they are…", canonical_key:"ch_11_closing_company_case_task_2_when_community", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"bd3a016f-0ba8-5550-ac6e-37bc7346658e", kc_id:"bd3a016f-0ba8-5550-ac6e-37bc7346658e", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 11, Closing Company Case, task 3. Case context: Adventist Health Castle Adventist Health Castle in Kailua, Hawaii, is an award-winning hospital focused on serving the mind, body, and spirit of its patients. The 300 physicians provide services to the entire island of Oahu, following the mission to “care for the community and share God’s love.”52 Adventist Health…. Learner task: Adventist Health Castle realized that access to health services was an important need in its community. To provide for that need, it developed a multidisciplinary clinic to serve rural communities. It immediately started seeing and treating patients. How does this fit into the service-profit chain?", label:"Ch. 11 Closing Company Case, task 3: Adventist Health Castle realized that access to health services was an important need…", canonical_key:"ch_11_closing_company_case_task_3_adventist_heal", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"a471b9b8-e2d1-5af5-b86d-fa67c295736a", kc_id:"a471b9b8-e2d1-5af5-b86d-fa67c295736a", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 11, Closing Company Case, task 4. Case context: Adventist Health Castle Adventist Health Castle in Kailua, Hawaii, is an award-winning hospital focused on serving the mind, body, and spirit of its patients. The 300 physicians provide services to the entire island of Oahu, following the mission to “care for the community and share God’s love.”52 Adventist Health…. Learner task: When Adventist Health Castle added more hours to physician practices, what dimension of service quality was it addressing be", label:"Ch. 11 Closing Company Case, task 4: When Adventist Health Castle added more hours to physician practices, what dimension…", canonical_key:"ch_11_closing_company_case_task_4_when_adventist", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"c833a0cf-f676-5ba4-ba6c-c67d6818d584", kc_id:"c833a0cf-f676-5ba4-ba6c-c67d6818d584", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 12, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 1. Learner task: Choose a mass retailer such as Walmart or Target and look at its weekly advertisement. You can do this online, in the store, or with a physical flyer. Identify and analyze the pricing strategies used. Apply what you have learned to how you personally respond to those strategies.", label:"Ch. 12 Discussion Questions, task 1: Choose a mass retailer such as Walmart or Target and look at its weekly advertisement", canonical_key:"ch_12_discussion_questions_task_1_choose_a_mass_", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"1beb982b-ab2b-5110-bf70-c628982043fe", kc_id:"1beb982b-ab2b-5110-bf70-c628982043fe", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 12, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 2. Learner task: Consider what products the penetration-price strategy and the price-skimming strategy work for. What are the advantages and disadvantages of these strategies?", label:"Ch. 12 Discussion Questions, task 2: Consider what products the penetration-price strategy and the price-skimming strategy…", canonical_key:"ch_12_discussion_questions_task_2_consider_what_", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"40700031-49db-5621-902e-4977dc131427", kc_id:"40700031-49db-5621-902e-4977dc131427", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 12, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 3. Learner task: Analyze the role pricing plays in strategic marketing.", label:"Ch. 12 Discussion Questions, task 3: Analyze the role pricing plays in strategic marketing.", canonical_key:"ch_12_discussion_questions_task_3_analyze_the_ro", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"aa982aa5-8432-5076-8ce1-559fd8570382", kc_id:"aa982aa5-8432-5076-8ce1-559fd8570382", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 12, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 4. Learner task: Discuss with your family and friends what you have learned about pricing. Ask them how they respond to odd-even pricing, prestige pricing, and artificial time constraints. Note generational differences and possibly how family traditions can skew the answers.", label:"Ch. 12 Discussion Questions, task 4: Discuss with your family and friends what you have learned about pricing", canonical_key:"ch_12_discussion_questions_task_4_discuss_with_y", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"bbb57a97-74c2-5c38-b0ea-17d3f1dd1eb9", kc_id:"bbb57a97-74c2-5c38-b0ea-17d3f1dd1eb9", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 12, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 1. Learner task: Compose a 150–200-word paragraph using all the following terms as they relate to pricing. The goal is to prove you understand the meaning of each term. Terms to include: • Unemployment • Inflation • Discretionary income • Consumer confidence", label:"Ch. 12 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 1: Compose a 150–200-word paragraph using all the following terms as they relate to pricing", canonical_key:"ch_12_critical_thinking_exercises_task_1_compose", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"73b1bf60-fac8-5cd0-a85f-98b5371310e7", kc_id:"73b1bf60-fac8-5cd0-a85f-98b5371310e7", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 12, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 2. Learner task: Describe a break-even point and provide a mathematical example.", label:"Ch. 12 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 2: Describe a break-even point and provide a mathematical example.", canonical_key:"ch_12_critical_thinking_exercises_task_2_describ", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"64935a3e-55fa-5ff2-8543-1ba1e819d707", kc_id:"64935a3e-55fa-5ff2-8543-1ba1e819d707", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 12, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 3. Learner task: Pick one product that you would find at a grocery store, a mass merchandiser, and a convenience store. Now go to each of these stores and check the price of the product you selected. Note if the product is on sale or listed at its regular price. Are the prices consistent? Is one store higher or lower across the board? What would compel a consumer to pay higher prices for products when they can purchase them at a lower price?", label:"Ch. 12 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 3: Pick one product that you would find at a grocery store, a mass merchandiser, and a…", canonical_key:"ch_12_critical_thinking_exercises_task_3_pick_on", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"da86f4fb-ed6e-5200-9cbd-17ffc7b349df", kc_id:"da86f4fb-ed6e-5200-9cbd-17ffc7b349df", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"create", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 12, Building Your Personal Brand, task 1. Learner task: One of the most important tasks you have in establishing your personal brand is how you are going to communicate your skill level and experience to others. Let’s start by developing a 30-second elevator pitch about yourself. An elevator pitch is what you would say about yourself if you were in an elevator with someone and only had the time between floors to share your message. What is the most important thing you would want to share about yourself and your personal brand if you were in an elevator with a hiring manager at company you want to work for? Things to consider covering include a quick introduction, your unique value or skill that would want to make them hire you, and something engaging about yourself to help them remember you.", label:"Ch. 12 Building Your Personal Brand, task 1: One of the most important tasks you have in establishing your personal brand is how…", canonical_key:"ch_12_building_your_personal_brand_task_1_one_of", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"bbd0a5b8-f2c9-5e16-970e-815e070d321d", kc_id:"bbd0a5b8-f2c9-5e16-970e-815e070d321d", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 12, What Do Marketers Do?, task 1. Learner task: Using LinkedIn, find a pricing analyst. Reach out to them, introduce yourself, and let them know that you’re a student wanting to know more about their job role. Then schedule an interview. Questions you may want to ask include: • What is your background and education, and what brought you to this job? • What do you feel are the pros and cons of this job role? • Share with me what a typical day, week, and year look like in this job role. • How has COVID-19 impacted your work? • What advice do you have for someone interested in pursuing this job?", label:"Ch. 12 What Do Marketers Do?, task 1: Using LinkedIn, find a pricing analyst", canonical_key:"ch_12_what_do_marketers_do_task_1_using_linkedin", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"77b735ae-2a82-5157-969f-dc3d8954e46d", kc_id:"77b735ae-2a82-5157-969f-dc3d8954e46d", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"create", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 12, Marketing Plan Exercise, task 1. Learner task: Complete the following information about the company and products/services you chose to focus on as you develop the marketing plan throughout the course. You may need to conduct research in order to obtain necessary information. Instructions: Using the Marketing Plan Template file you created from the Marketing and Customer Value assignment and expanded upon in Strategic Planning in Marketing, Market Segmentation, Targeting, and Positioning, Marketing Research and Market Intelligence, and Products: Consumer Offerings, complete the following section of your marketing plan: • Marketing Strategy: Pricing Submit the marketing plan to your instructor for grading and feedback.", label:"Ch. 12 Marketing Plan Exercise, task 1: Complete the following information about the company and products/services you chose…", canonical_key:"ch_12_marketing_plan_exercise_task_1_complete_th", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"07534b7a-86c4-5773-83f9-bc3a7a377ff6", kc_id:"07534b7a-86c4-5773-83f9-bc3a7a377ff6", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 12, Closing Company Case, task 1. Case context: Naked Wines Buying a good bottle of wine can be hit or miss. A consumer can pay a lot and not enjoy the wine or pay a little and really love the wine. As with any product, there are fixed costs and variable costs included in the price of a bottle of wine. Some of those expenses include the costs of production, the…. Learner task: What are the psychological factors that affect the pricing of wine?", label:"Ch. 12 Closing Company Case, task 1: What are the psychological factors that affect the pricing of wine", canonical_key:"ch_12_closing_company_case_task_1_what_are_the_p", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"9bc17d58-3e64-5dde-88ba-6702f8024f2d", kc_id:"9bc17d58-3e64-5dde-88ba-6702f8024f2d", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 12, Closing Company Case, task 2. Case context: Naked Wines Buying a good bottle of wine can be hit or miss. A consumer can pay a lot and not enjoy the wine or pay a little and really love the wine. As with any product, there are fixed costs and variable costs included in the price of a bottle of wine. Some of those expenses include the costs of production, the…. Learner task: Name the five critical Cs of pricing evident in the Naked Wines pricing model.", label:"Ch. 12 Closing Company Case, task 2: Name the five critical Cs of pricing evident in the Naked Wines pricing model.", canonical_key:"ch_12_closing_company_case_task_2_name_the_five_", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"a7e64c74-2b0e-56a5-8c0f-e66be6801213", kc_id:"a7e64c74-2b0e-56a5-8c0f-e66be6801213", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 12, Closing Company Case, task 3. Case context: Naked Wines Buying a good bottle of wine can be hit or miss. A consumer can pay a lot and not enjoy the wine or pay a little and really love the wine. As with any product, there are fixed costs and variable costs included in the price of a bottle of wine. Some of those expenses include the costs of production, the…. Learner task: What 