falls of paid sponsorships. Occasionally an issue hits the news about something that had a blowback effect on the company that sponsored a team, event, and/or product.", label:"Ch. 13 Discussion Questions, task 4: Identify some of the benefits and the pitfalls of paid sponsorships", canonical_key:"ch_13_discussion_questions_task_4_identify_some_", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"81102a5f-4d8c-5285-a233-ea8868ba8cad", kc_id:"81102a5f-4d8c-5285-a233-ea8868ba8cad", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 13, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 1. Learner task: Compose a 150–200-word paragraph using all the following terms as they relate to integrated marketing communications. The goal is to prove you understand the meaning of each term. Terms: • advertising • digital marketing • frequency • reach • feedback loop • sales promotion", label:"Ch. 13 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 1: Compose a 150–200-word paragraph using all the following terms as they relate to…", canonical_key:"ch_13_critical_thinking_exercises_task_1_compose", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"ab646678-d52c-5880-b9a2-75d3b47d3378", kc_id:"ab646678-d52c-5880-b9a2-75d3b47d3378", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 13, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 2. Learner task: Several companies come to mind when we think about great integrated marketing communications; Target and Gap are two of those. Consider other companies that have campaigns that you recognize in any form of marketing that truly stand out. What makes them memorable?", label:"Ch. 13 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 2: Several companies come to mind when we think about great integrated marketing…", canonical_key:"ch_13_critical_thinking_exercises_task_2_several", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"bbdb2d12-6a22-5a61-9475-7bf430c9b7ea", kc_id:"bbdb2d12-6a22-5a61-9475-7bf430c9b7ea", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 13, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 3. Learner task: Socially responsible marketing campaigns such as the Subaru one mentioned are becoming more visible over time. Identify two to three other campaigns that you have seen. What do they use as a motivator? Is it to give to a cause, to buy a product or service that they sell based on the fact that they make a donation in your name, or is it simply an informative campaign?", label:"Ch. 13 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 3: Socially responsible marketing campaigns such as the Subaru one mentioned are becoming…", canonical_key:"ch_13_critical_thinking_exercises_task_3_sociall", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"628c7981-6e27-5fc9-8826-cc75d212ac50", kc_id:"628c7981-6e27-5fc9-8826-cc75d212ac50", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"create", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 13, Building Your Personal Brand, task 1. Learner task: One of the key ways that you can build your personal brand is by association. The following is a list of marketing associations. Research each of these to determine which organization(s) are most congruent with your goals. Many of these organizations have local chapters that you can join, where you can attend a function, or that you can simply use to gather additional information. These are great ways to network with other marketing professionals, organizations, and industry leaders. From this association you can continue to develop a 