:"ch_14_critical_thinking_exercises_task_4_provide", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"13e2608b-33f8-57c5-83d2-2b3c0a06d512", kc_id:"13e2608b-33f8-57c5-83d2-2b3c0a06d512", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"create", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 14, Building Your Personal Brand, task 1. Learner task: The act of building a personal brand requires a commitment that comes with having a well-developed and clear path. One of the many tools that a person can use to set and review their progress is the GOOD framework from Quantum Workplace (https://openstax.org/r/quantumworkplace). This framework can be used to set goals, identify obstacles and opportunities, and make decisions. As with any strategic goal-setting framework, the important thing to remember is that it should be used organically, allowing for the shifts that come with growth and development. The framework includes the following parts: • Goals: What goals are you setting? What needs to be done to achieve them? • Obstacles: What is standing in your way? Can you work around or remove the…", label:"Ch. 14 Building Your Personal Brand, task 1: The act of building a personal brand requires a commitment that comes with having a…", canonical_key:"ch_14_building_your_personal_brand_task_1_the_ac", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"cc6bee86-e88e-58f5-8692-2a7c7604f7d7", kc_id:"cc6bee86-e88e-58f5-8692-2a7c7604f7d7", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 14, What Do Marketers Do?, task 1. Case context: Send a message to your college or university marketing department asking for a time to talk to the marketing manager about their job for your class. These positions vary greatly based on how many functions they outsource. Use the following questions as a guide to dig deeper into their process and responsibilities.. Learner task: Please share with me your employment history and how you got to where you are today.", label:"Ch. 14 What Do Marketers Do?, task 1: Please share with me your employment history and how you got to where you are today.", canonical_key:"ch_14_what_do_marketers_do_task_1_please_share_w", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"0b21f7d9-d00f-56ad-9b77-fa28e13830c8", kc_id:"0b21f7d9-d00f-56ad-9b77-fa28e13830c8", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 14, What Do Marketers Do?, task 2. Case context: Send a message to your college or university marketing department asking for a time to talk to the marketing manager about their job for your class. These positions vary greatly based on how many functions they outsource. Use the following questions as a guide to dig deeper into their process and responsibilities.. Learner task: Can you summarize your job responsibilities?", label:"Ch. 14 What Do Marketers Do?, task 2: Can you summarize your job responsibilities", canonical_key:"ch_14_what_do_marketers_do_task_2_can_you_summar", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"90b7338c-a76e-5833-9d2c-3edf70e10ab8", kc_id:"90b7338c-a76e-5833-9d2c-3edf70e10ab8", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 14, What Do Marketers Do?, task 3. Case context: Send a message to your college or university marketing department asking for a time to talk to the marketing manager about their job for your class. These positions vary greatly based on how many functions they outsource. Use the following questions as a guide to dig deeper into their process and responsibilities.. Learner task: Is the organizational structure of the company you work for private, nonprofit, or state?", label:"Ch. 14 What Do Marketers Do?, task 3: Is the organizational structure of the company you work for private, nonprofit, or state", canonical_key:"ch_14_what_do_marketers_do_task_3_is_the_organiz", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"ac7bdd84-cf01-54e4-a2fa-467b31fb3322", kc_id:"ac7bdd84-cf01-54e4-a2fa-467b31fb3322", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"create", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 14, What Do Marketers Do?, task 4. Case context: Send a message to your college or university marketing department asking for a time to talk to the marketing manager about their job for your class. These positions vary greatly based on how many functions they outsource. Use the following questions as a guide to dig deeper into their process and responsibilities.. Learner task: Can you share with me what functions, if any, are outsourced (for example, website design, website maintenance, graphic design, or printing of materials)? How long have you been outsourcing these functions?", label:"Ch. 14 What Do Marketers Do?, task 4: Can you share with me what functions, if any, are outsourced (for example, website…", canonical_key:"ch_14_what_do_marketers_do_task_4_can_you_share_", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"f3335752-7c1c-5cae-a4b4-8b49703de60b", kc_id:"f3335752-7c1c-5cae-a4b4-8b49703de60b", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 14, What Do Marketers Do?, task 5. Case context: Send a message to your college or university marketing department asking for a time to talk to the marketing manager about their job for your class. These positions vary greatly based on how many functions they outsource. Use the following questions as a guide to dig deeper into their process and responsibilities.. Learner task: How many employees report to you, and what is person’s role?", label:"Ch. 14 What Do Marketers Do?, task 5: How many employees report to you, and what is person’s role", canonical_key:"ch_14_what_do_marketers_do_task_5_how_many_emplo", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"bb80d99b-f2e2-5f1e-9320-2c12e33bc318", kc_id:"bb80d99b-f2e2-5f1e-9320-2c12e33bc318", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 14, What Do Marketers Do?, task 6. Case context: Send a message to your college or university marketing department asking for a time to talk to the marketing manager about their job for your class. These positions vary greatly based on how many functions they outsource. Use the following questions as a guide to dig deeper into their process and responsibilities.. Learner task: What challenges do you face with the structure you currently have in place? Feel free to add any questions you might have. Thank them for their time. From this interview you should be able to gain more insight into how different areas of marketing are handled within a given organization’s marketing department.", label:"Ch. 14 What Do Marketers Do?, task 6: What challenges do you face with the structure you currently have in place", canonical_key:"ch_14_what_do_marketers_do_task_6_what_challenge", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"7c1f3c35-02a6-56b0-b425-f613dd5f4b60", kc_id:"7c1f3c35-02a6-56b0-b425-f613dd5f4b60", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in c