tions that you have participated in. List them and the product that they were used to promote. Did you buy the product based on the promotion? If you did, what was the selling point? If you did not, where did it miss the mark? Pick a product that you are familiar with, and create a promotion aimed at the consumer.", label:"Ch. 15 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 2: Consider the promotions that you have participated in", canonical_key:"ch_15_critical_thinking_exercises_task_2_conside", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"99dee407-b91a-5f75-b977-42d0001e8103", kc_id:"99dee407-b91a-5f75-b977-42d0001e8103", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 15, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 3. Learner task: Identify a time you’ve read about or were personally involved in an unethical sales experience.", label:"Ch. 15 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 3: Identify a time you’ve read about or were personally involved in an unethical sales…", canonical_key:"ch_15_critical_thinking_exercises_task_3_identif", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"716a450d-35ce-5109-9915-1a76cf50ea68", kc_id:"716a450d-35ce-5109-9915-1a76cf50ea68", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"create", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 15, Building Your Personal Brand, task 1. Learner task: Consider the concept of personal selling, and apply it to yourself. What information would you need? How would you go about crafting your message? First, gather the facts that you would like someone to know about you, and create a list. Next, craft the basic “elevator pitch” introduction (that is, you only have an elevator ride to tell someone your unique value). What would that pitch include? Next, make a list of the situations where you might need an introduction (sales pitch) that is longer and contains more detail. Consider a job interview (much of this information should be on your resume), joining a club or professional organization, or volunteering. Each of these situations calls for slightly different information. Create several different…", label:"Ch. 15 Building Your Personal Brand, task 1: Consider the concept of personal selling, and apply it to yourself", canonical_key:"ch_15_building_your_personal_brand_task_1_consid", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"a98875f4-eae7-51cf-b49a-68ebced201ed", kc_id:"a98875f4-eae7-51cf-b49a-68ebced201ed", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 15, What Do Marketers Do?, task 1. Case context: We are surrounded by personal selling encounters: cell phone, insurance, services in a bank, restaurant, and the list goes on. Pick a service that you would like to learn more about. Now find a person that holds the job of personally selling that service/product. Reach out to them; you can call, walk into a business,…. Learner task: Start with simple information. What does the job entail?", label:"Ch. 15 What Do Marketers Do?, task 1: Start with simple information", canonical_key:"ch_15_what_do_marketers_do_task_1_start_with_sim", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"d3c908e7-6663-52b6-9576-3479e4a129ca", kc_id:"d3c908e7-6663-52b6-9576-3479e4a129ca", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 15, What Do Marketers Do?, task 2. Case context: We are surrounded by personal selling encounters: cell phone, insurance, services in a bank, restaurant, and the list goes on. Pick a service that you would like to learn more about. Now find a person that holds the job of personally selling that service/product. Reach out to them; you can call, walk into a business,…. Learner task: How did they get the job? How long have they been doing personal selling?", label:"Ch. 15 What Do Marketers Do?, task 2: How did they get the job", canonical_key:"ch_15_what_do_marketers_do_task_2_how_did_they_g", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"93780976-df66-5aaa-8f1f-dd539191006c", kc_id:"93780976-df66-5aaa-8f1f-dd539191006c", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 15, What Do Marketers Do?, task 3. Case context: We are surrounded by personal selling encounters: cell phone, insurance, services in a bank, restaurant, and the list goes on. Pick a service that you would like to learn more about. Now find a person that holds the job of personally selling that service/product. Reach out to them; you can call, walk into a business,…. Learner task: Do they enjoy what they do? What are the best parts and the worst parts of the job?", label:"Ch. 15 What Do Marketers Do?, task 3: Do they enjoy what they do", canonical_key:"ch_15_what_do_marketers_do_task_3_do_they_enjoy_", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"167d905d-f29f-5573-b8c8-3a1f8741756a", kc_id:"167d905d-f29f-5573-b8c8-3a1f8741756a", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 15, What Do Marketers Do?, task 4. Case context: We are surrounded by personal selling encounters: cell phone, insurance, services in a bank, restaurant, and the list goes on. Pick a service that you would like to learn more about. Now find a person that holds the job of personally selling that service/produ