k 2. Learner task: Choose three people that you know, each from a different generation. Explain the concept of online, social media, and mobile marketing. Ask the following questions: “Do you engage with these forms of marketing?” “Have you purchased anything from one of these forms?” “Do you have any concerns about using any of the marketing strategies discussed?” Then, explain whether anyone’s answers surprised you.", label:"Ch. 16 Discussion Questions, task 2: Choose three people that you know, each from a different generation", canonical_key:"ch_16_discussion_questions_task_2_choose_three_p", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"a6f90ed4-7d4a-52d0-8e9b-9d43234e1838", kc_id:"a6f90ed4-7d4a-52d0-8e9b-9d43234e1838", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 16, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 3. Learner task: When considering the privacy issue, where does the responsibility fall? Is it with the business, or is it with the consumer? Is it both? How can a consumer guard themselves? What can a company do to make sure it is practicing ethical marketing?", label:"Ch. 16 Discussion Questions, task 3: When considering the privacy issue, where does the responsibility fall", canonical_key:"ch_16_discussion_questions_task_3_when_consideri", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"0bba18d3-82a9-59d0-9107-b24b8313d9ff", kc_id:"0bba18d3-82a9-59d0-9107-b24b8313d9ff", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 16, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 4. Learner task: The main goals of consumer protection laws and regulations are to protect consumers’ privacy and identity and to protect consumers