UNWIND [{concept_id:"fa4f5c73-e163-598f-867f-4995937fc034", kc_id:"fa4f5c73-e163-598f-867f-4995937fc034", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 16, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 2. Learner task: List the positive and negative value of each of these forms of marketing: direct mail, social media, mobile, content and telemarketing. Think about products, messages, and delivery systems.", label:"Ch. 16 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 2: List the positive and negative value of each of these forms of marketing: direct mail,…", canonical_key:"ch_16_critical_thinking_exercises_task_2_list_th", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"3f26f763-82c6-5e82-9401-e8bbdf84ac05", kc_id:"3f26f763-82c6-5e82-9401-e8bbdf84ac05", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 16, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 3. Learner task: Now consider the target market for direct mail, social media, mobile, content marketing, and telemarketing. Does the chosen form of marketing present challenges in growing the target market? If so, how can those challenges be met and overcome?", label:"Ch. 16 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 3: Now consider the target market for direct mail, social media, mobile, content…", canonical_key:"ch_16_critical_thinking_exercises_task_3_now_con", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"6e85aa24-fb74-57a6-bfbf-35634b423cf9", kc_id:"6e85aa24-fb74-57a6-bfbf-35634b423cf9", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"create", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 16, Building Your Personal Brand, task 1. Learner task: Goal-setting is the development of an action plan designed to motivate and guide an individual, group, or organization to reach a goal. There are several models of goal setting; one of the popular ones is SMART goal- setting. SMART stands for goals that are specific, measurable, action-oriented, realistic, and time-bound. Consider a goal you might set for yourself that’s SMART. For example, if your goal is to intern at a marketing firm ,you might establish the following SMART goals: • Specific: Create a list of possible companies you want to target for an internship, and indicate why. • Measurable: Quantify the number of contacts at each company you plan to make in a week, and map those to calendar dates. • Action-oriented: Develop a plan for…", label:"Ch. 16 Building Your Personal Brand, task 1: Goal-setting is the development of an action plan designed to motivate and guide an…", canonical_key:"ch_16_building_your_personal_brand_task_1_goal_s", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"d66d6962-7f05-5a46-8db9-b3faeacccecb", kc_id:"d66d6962-7f05-5a46-8db9-b3faeacccecb", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"create", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 16, What Do Marketers Do?, task 1. Learner task: Check out the Association of National Advertisers (ANA) website (https://openstax.org/r/ananet), and scan the wealth of information available. It offers a content library, newsstand, marketing futures, blogs, and podcasts. Throughout this information, you will learn more about many aspects of current trends, future opportunities, and simply what it is that marketers are doing now. Being educated on the many associations and the information available can inspire you to look at marketing careers in a different light. Navigate to the Content Library, then the Media Channels section. (In order to see the link to the Content Library, you need to hover over “Resources” at the top of the page.) From this section, review the various pieces of content…", label:"Ch. 16 What Do Marketers Do?, task 1: Check out the Association of National Advertisers (ANA) website…", canonical_key:"ch_16_what_do_marketers_do_task_1_check_out_the_", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"e5f94f9e-d923-5fb2-b25c-b3ca41141954", kc_id:"e5f94f9e-d923-5fb2-b25c-b3ca41141954", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 16, Closing Company Case, task 1. Case context: Publix Founded in 1930, supermarket chain Publix started with one store in Winter Haven, Florida. It now has over 1,200 stores throughout the Southeast. The company was founded on the promise of superior customer service. With unwavering dedication to quality and value, Publix is now one of the 10 largest-volume…. Learner task: Describe the ways Publix is utilizing its website to connect with customers.", label:"Ch. 16 Closing Company Case, task 1: Describe the ways Publix is utilizing its website to connect with customers.", canonical_key:"ch_16_closing_company_case_task_1_describe_the_w", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"28c0936c-50f6-5607-bb48-f2a25159a662", kc_id:"28c0936c-50f6-5607-bb48-f2a25159a662", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 16, Closing Company Case, task 2. Case context: Publix Founded in 1930, supermarket chain Publix started with one store in Winter Haven, Florida. It now has over 1,200 stores throughout the Southeast. The company was founded on the promise of superior customer service. With unwavering dedication to quality and value, Publix is now one of the 10 largest-volume…. Le