e direct consumer marketing channels and indirect consumer marketing channels. List an example of each type and explain the difference between them.", label:"Ch. 18 Discussion Questions, task 1: Define direct consumer marketing channels and indirect consumer marketing channels", canonical_key:"ch_18_discussion_questions_task_1_define_direct_", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"3ba7bdc1-f268-5440-b0d9-e3b4d2ce1a06", kc_id:"3ba7bdc1-f268-5440-b0d9-e3b4d2ce1a06", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 18, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 2. Learner task: The shift to online shopping has challenged many retailers who had only a brick-and-mortar location. One of the industries hit hardest by changes in consumer behavior is travel agencies because travelers can access much of the necessary pricing information themselves and then purchase tickets directly from the airlines. Name two additional store retailers that have virtually disappeared because of non-store retailing.", label:"Ch. 18 Discussion Questions, task 2: The shift to online shopping has challenged many retailers who had only a…", canonical_key:"ch_18_discussion_questions_task_2_the_shift_to_o", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"96e3ad23-1fa8-5562-8fea-a501051ca18c", kc_id:"96e3ad23-1fa8-5562-8fea-a501051ca18c", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 18, Applied Marketing Knowledge: Discussion Questions, task 3. Learner task: Markup is a term used by retailers to explain how much revenue comes from the difference between the cost of acquiring a product and the price it is sold for. Why do florists usually mark up their products 8