ept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 18, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 1. Learner task: According to PR Newswire, more than 40 percent of the overall revenue from the multimodal distribution market is due to roadway logistics. Give three reasons why retailers and wholesalers depend largely on roads—rather than rail, air, or water—to send and receive products. Why do roads create the greatest transportation-based revenue for businesses and lowest costs for consumers?", label:"Ch. 18 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 1: According to PR Newswire, more than 40 percent of the overall revenue from the…", canonical_key:"ch_18_critical_thinking_exercises_task_1_accordi", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"b7e5f12b-8248-51da-96e4-892aebdf0087", kc_id:"b7e5f12b-8248-51da-96e4-892aebdf0087", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 18, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 2. Learner task: Thanks to retailers and wholesalers and their strategies, products may be distributed in various ways. What are two examples of consumer products that are sold by retailers, and what is the corresponding distribution strategy?", label:"Ch. 18 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 2: Thanks to retailers and wholesalers and their strategies, products may be distributed…", canonical_key:"ch_18_critical_thinking_exercises_task_2_thanks_", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"af7f9187-54b6-5136-bf6c-9e829670b979", kc_id:"af7f9187-54b6-5136-bf6c-9e829670b979", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"evaluate", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 18, Critical Thinking Exercises, task 3. Learner task: Most firms today take advantage of multimodal transportation, especially those that source and distribute products internationally. List three reasons why multimodal transportation makes sense financially for a retailer like Amazon that operates in a time-sensitive marketplace.", label:"Ch. 18 Critical Thinking Exercises, task 3: Most firms today take advantage of multimodal transportation, especially those that…", canonical_key:"ch_18_critical_thinking_exercises_task_3_most_fi", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"9af71941-a83b-5599-adfb-dbcd6986847f", kc_id:"9af71941-a83b-5599-adfb-dbcd6986847f", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"create", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 18, Building Your Personal Brand, task 1. Learner task: Have you ever worked in a grocery store stocking shelves, worked at your campus bookstore, or waited on customers at a restaurant or drive-through? Working in retail is a fantastic resume booster. Not only have you advanced your knowledge of the business world, but you have also worked closely with demanding customers and management in a retail environment. Learning to serve customers, following training and rules, being part of a successful job interview, and holding a job outside of school are all highly coveted experiences. According to the Skills You Need website, the most important employability skills include “getting along with and working well with other people” and “being reliable and dependable: doing what you say you will by the deadline…", label:"Ch. 18 Building Your Personal Brand, task 1: Have you ever worked in a grocery store stocking shelves, worked at your campus…", canonical_key:"ch_18_building_your_personal_brand_task_1_have_y", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"4ee77682-f810-5c44-a314-3b3938ee2dd8", kc_id:"4ee77682-f810-5c44-a314-3b3938ee2dd8", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"analyze", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 18, What Do Marketers Do?, task 1. Learner task: C.H. Robinson is a third-party logistics provider headquartered in Eden Prairie, Minnesota. Many businesses outsource elements of distribution, warehousing, and fulfillment services to companies such as C.H. Robinson. Like wholesalers, logistics providers, also an intrinsic part of the value delivery system, operate largely outside of the public eye. Reach out to one of the 297 C.H. Robinson locations and ask if you can speak to someone about recent supply chain trends for a college course assignment. Your questions may include the following: • How does technology impact the supply chain? • What is the biggest industry you work with that depends on supply chain partners? • How has the COVID-19 pandemic impacted product availability and distribution…", label:"Ch. 18 What Do Marketers Do?, task 1: C.H", canonical_key:"ch_18_what_do_marketers_do_task_1_c_h", status:"approved"}}, {concept_id:"5547e51f-2d4c-5af4-8b6e-87b61371c1fe", kc_id:"5547e51f-2d4c-5af4-8b6e-87b61371c1fe", properties:{course_id:"8a9fefac-e5b9-49dd-935c-88cfd1929e26", bloom_level:"create", updated_at:datetime('2026-09-20T10:16:37.749Z'), level:"atomic_concept", concept_type:"method", definition:"Source assessment in chapter 18, Marketing Plan Exercise, task 1. Learner task: Complete the following information about the company and products/services you chose to focus on as you develop the marketing plan throughout the course. You may need to conduct research in order to obtain the necessary information. Instructions: Using the Marketing Plan Template file you created from the Marketing and Customer Value assignment and expanded upon in Strategic Planning in Marketing, Market Segmentation, Targeting, and Positioning, Marketing Research and Market Intelligence, Products: Consumer Offerings, Pricing Products and Services, Integrated Mar